<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-export SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/evernote-export4.dtd">
<en-export export-date="20260208T005625Z" application="Evernote" version="11.1.2">
  <note>
    <title>Rune 2019 Campaign Hooks</title>
    <created>20190710T151623Z</created>
    <updated>20230906T224939Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Plot Points: </div><ul><li><div>The party is asked to drive off some squatters that are sitting on Tal’Aeowan’s land. She can’t get there because she’s needed in the city to handle council matters. Charlie’s character’s family sends him, and they recruit help. </div></li><li><div>The squatters are goblins who were trained by Torg, Charlie’s old assassin character. They have basic ranger, trapping, &amp; sniping skills. The land is also turning to swampland due to Zel’s influence. </div></li><li><div>When the party fails or realizes they are in over their head, their return to Ghealdar sparks a city-council commitment to sweep all squatters: goblins, orcs operating illegal prostitution/alcohol vendor stalls, and elves who are sleeping in the streets. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Ghealdar has descended into economic chaos and the Orcish nation of Gibard has stepped in to keep the peace, protect their citizens and the property of their citizens. They support the city council continuing to be in charge, but they are the muscle that makes it happen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Ghealdarian families who survived the chaos have limited production of food and other supplies, keeping themselves safe and driving prices to rapacious levels. </div><div><br/></div><div>On top of all of this, a handful of Atanian goblin Engineers and entrepreneurs have set up shop in Atania, creating a goblin mall, full of goblin curiosities and fetishes that Ghealdarian citizens with money like to collect. They also deal in occasional black market merchandise. The challenge is that all contracts with all goblins are canceled, and new ones cannot be entered with goblins, so making money is a challenge for these entrepreneurs. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Tuatha De Danaan are active in Ghealdar as guerrilla fighters, teaming up with goblins and humans to teach them how to fight the orcs. Poor goblins and humans are being recruited as suicide attackers, with knives and even the occasional magical bomb. </div><div><br/></div><div>All of this somehow leads to the party confronting a duo of hatchling black dragons after a storm. CR 2 each. The dragon hatchlings are hungry and scared and try to eat the party. If the party attacks and kills them, their older sister (Young Adult CR 7) finds their bodies and hunts down the party. It might take her a while, to let the party level up. There’s a confrontation and either way, that dragon goes back to the Council of Dragons and raises the alarm about the state of humanity. A group of dragons decides to go rogue and eliminate the human threat. The Sidhe had it right with the Gaeas, but they didn’t go far enough. The destruction of Ghealdar is imminent, followed shortly after by Atania and Gibard. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Free States have already closed their border to goblins. There are encampments at the borders, with neighboring city-states arguing over who's land they are on, and who is responsible for them. This could rise to a level of tension that leads to violence. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>What are the former goblin party members doing? </div></li><ul><li><div>Torg (Charlie’s character) is living in the swamp with Zel, the black dragon. He is training goblins and creating his own private army. </div></li><li><div>After 5 years, Juice is fairly certain he was right in the first place that “gentle slavery” wasn’t such a bad thing. By abandoning the love and compassion of the Creator and allowing himself to be seduced by the spirits of slain Goblins (who he now sees as motivated by simple vengeance and not any kind of wish for a brighter tomorrow) Juice became a powerful force for bringing down the standard of living for not only Goblins, but everyone in the Kingdom who took part in the economy. He spends his days in despair, mostly NOT eating, praying to hear the voice of a Creator who appears to be punishing him. villainous- of a third movement).  In their mind the orcs are basically taking over, and that can’t be a good thing in the long run. The elves are sowing chaos for their own expansion, without a real plan for how to manage the vacuum that will follow for everyone else. Juice thinks the old system worked fine as long as those power and money were taking care of those without.  The lack of individual freedom for goblins was simply a price to pay for this security. If society  could get back to a place where the rich were using their wealth to care for the poor, and everyone was employed and not looting, that’s a win in his book.  It needs to come back in a way where goblins have a little more agency.  Maybe juice’s faction are the guys pushing for reparations?  That would be one way of taking the wealth of the rich and putting it in the hands of those that need it most. Although honestly he has found the world a little scary ever since leaving the estate, and there is something comforting about having a master to take care of all that for you…</div></li></ul><ul><li><div>Nocke (if she isn't dead, I straight up can't remember) would either be finding the magic devices that are now lost, originally made for Goblin Freedom - or she would be going from city to city with a small contingency of whoever to give speeches to sway crowds that while the Goblins are free, they are still not equal: looking for benefactors, business owners, and philanthropists to start new ventures in Ghaeldar hiring Goblins, helping them start their own businesses without basically indentured servitude or unplayable contracts, and or give money to a fund she's started for help in Ghaeldar.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="-en-paragraph:true;">Ghealdar's economy is circling the drain and violence has erupted. The orcish nation of Gibard has sent a peacekeeping force to protect its citizens’ interests and property. The Ghealdar city council is nominally still in charge, but tensions are high. </span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="-en-paragraph:true;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">A brief history of Ghealdar</span></span></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="-en-paragraph:true;">The second largest city in the Free States, Ghealder was left a smoking ruin after the Hartland war. Cyric the Warlord devastated the Fey Court's Eladrin army there and the Summer Queen retaliated by sending her most powerful general, Badb, to decimate the city. Cyric took advantage of the hundreds of newly dead by enslaving their bodies and spirits in horrific undeath. 
</span></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="-en-paragraph:true;">For 200 years after Cyric was brought down, the city laid abandoned. The tribes of the plains avoided the city with the exception of the handful of foolhardy warriors on vision quests.  </span></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">To reclaim their ancestral home, The Reconcilers led a coalition of forces from the newly established Free States to cleanse the city of the planar rift leading to the Shadowfell. After that, the city thrived under the leadership of a diverse council. The city became a marvelous meld of magic and mechanics. </div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="-en-paragraph:true;">Five years ago, a group of goblins led a city-wide protest against slavery. The official story is that the goblins found a sympathetic ally in Rutherford, a wealthy and powerful gnomish wizard. Rutherford, in his final days, pushed for the release of goblins from the bonds of slavery. His dying wishes were honored by the city council, but that decision has resulted in disaster. The unofficial story is only whispered but involves a team of goblin covert operatives forcing the city council's hand through blackmail.</span></div><div>The goblins were immediately given their freedom. No more slavery. A large percentage left, some going to Atania and the Free States, until these nations closed their border to goblin refugees. Some returned to their ancestral homeland in the mountains only to discover their feral cousins were not as welcoming. Those goblins ended up becoming sharecroppers in Gibard, the Orcish kingdom, or setting up their own hopeless camps in the rugged mountains of the Dragonspine.</div><div><br/></div><div>Of those who stayed, most of the goblins still live in The Dump. There’s been some talk of giving goblins education and land, but nothing has happened. Many shopkeepers have closed up, claiming they cannot pay their goblin employees. Many goblins are more poor now because they no longer have benefactors and the Dump is overflowing with bodies of the dead and nearly dead. Drug use is rampant. </div><div><br/></div><div>Of the wealthy families that were slaveholders, several of them left the city out of fear of retribution. Their absence caused a cascade of business failures. The orcs already in Ghealdar tried to step in to fill those gaps, but the Tuatha Dé, a secret cabal of elven freedom fighters, began quietly undermining and damaging those businesses. A handful of goblins have prospered, but most of them have no education and have succumbed to despair or lives of crime. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Important NPCs &amp; organizations</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">Aaron Featherington</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">was one of Seamus' direct reports. He lost his job when Seamus fell on hard times. He has drifted from master to master looking for work, dabbling in a protection racket that keeps a small sector of Ghealdar free of violence. </span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;"><span style="line-height: 100%; font-weight: bold;">Tuatha Dé Danaan</span> - the elves who have fought guerrilla warfare against Gibard saw an opportunity when Ghealdar’s economy collapsed and began attacking orcish business interests throughout Ghealdar. Nobody has been able to catch any members of the terrorist cell and their existence is without evidence. </span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Tal’Eowan</span> is an elven former blade singer, now a member of the city council, the only one to survive the collapse of the city’s economy. She was rumored to traffic in the drug trade but those rumors have faded as she has worked tirelessly to improve the lives of average Ghealdarians.</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Zel</span> - a young adult black dragon who previously lived underneath Rutherford’s mansion but now occupies a swamp miles East of the city. This dragon has mysteriously allied itself with a handful of goblin criminals, protecting them from law enforcement. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">Seamus O’Connell </span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">was one of the most prominent slaveholders. He owned the contracts on scores of goblins</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">. His fortune took a devastating blow after the goblin freedom, but he has managed to hold on to his real estate holdings, renting them out to the Gibardian orcs. He is sought after by those who want to deal with the orcs. His manor grounds in Ghealdar are home to several wargs and other unsavory creatures. </span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">Finn Aero </span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">is</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;"> a human fence who made it through the upheaval by working with nearly everyone, laundering antiquities and other hot goods. Finn is a mild-mannered character, but he is rumored to have dealings with privateers who work for Atania. </span>The shipyard thieves guild, <span style="font-weight: bold;">The Sharks</span>, takes a cut of most of the trade in and out of the port, and in the city, <span style="font-weight: bold;">Meirlich</span> is a tight organization of thieves who do high-profile cons on unsuspecting folks. Both groups leverage Finn's connections to have high-powered lawyers that enforce contracts and get their people out of jail.</div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="line-height: 100%; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">The Ghealdar Goblin Underground Freedom Force </span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">is a group of goblins and goblin allies who are working to help Ghealdarian goblins find education and economic prosperity.  </span></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="line-height: 100%; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Sarge</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">is the twin brother of Religieuse. They're enormous goblins. Where Religieuse is fat and clumsy, Sarge is muscular underneath his layer of fat. He was a slave owned by one of Tal'Eowan's captains, a human named Sledge. Sarge acts as a bouncer for Sledge's night clubs. </span></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="line-height: 100%; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Mhamo</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;"> is the goblin grandmother. She is a mysterious figure who used to arrange for goblins to disappear from Ghealdar, and now helps them sneak into neighboring countries. She is an old, wrinkled goblin that very few people have actually seen.
</span></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="line-height: 100%; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Grok</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">us the pseudonym used by a loose group of goblin engineers and wizards from Atania who are trying to help Mhamo get the Ghealdarian goblins out or to find resources. The magic devices they previously built for freedom fighting have been lost or sold. They have recently reappeared in several high-profile attacks against the orcs. </span></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="line-height: 100%; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Filch</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">is part of a street gang run by Shadow. He's a consummate sneak. He can infiltrate anything – probably with the help of some kind of magic. His street gang helps Mhamo – but Shadow has secret connections to the biggest crime boss, Finn Aero. Shadow is Finn's slave, and Finn pays her very, very well for her information.</span><span style="line-height: 100%;-en-paragraph:true;">
</span></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>The Great Djinn</title>
    <created>20210302T053339Z</created>
    <updated>20230906T224937Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>DJINN 1 - AIR</div><div><br/></div><h1><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Barqan, Djinni Sorceror 12</span></b></h1><div style="text-align:start;"><i><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Large elemental, chaotic good</span></i></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Armor Class </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">17 (Natural Armor)</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Hit Points </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">161 (14d10+84)</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Speed </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">30 ft., fly 90 ft.</span></div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">STR </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">21 (+5)  </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">DEX </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">15 (+2) </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">CON </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">22 (+6) </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">INT </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">15 (+2)  </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">WIS </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">16 (+3) </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">CHA </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">24 (+6)</span></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Saving Throws </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Dex +9, Wis +12, Cha +15</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Damage Immunities </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Lightning, Thunder</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Senses </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Darkvision 120 Ft., passive Perception 13</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Languages </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Auran, common </span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Challenge </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">11 (7,200 XP)</span></div></li></ul><div><br/></div><ul><li><div><b><i><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Elemental Demise</span></i></b><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">. If the djinni dies, its body disintegrates into a warm breeze, leaving behind only equipment the djinni was wearing or carrying</span></div></li><li><div><b><i><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Innate Spellcasting</span></i></b><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">. The djinni's innate spellcasting ability is Charisma (spell save DC 20, +9 to hit with spell attacks). It can innately cast the following spells, requiring no material components: • At will: detect evil and good, detect magic, thunderwave • 3/day each: create food and water (can create wine instead of water), tongues, wind walk • 1/day each: conjure elemental (air elemental only), creation, gaseous form, invisibility, major image, plane shift**</span></div></li><li><div><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">1/day each: Mass Suggestion, Freezing Sphere, Wall of Force, Hold Monster, Cone of Cold, Greater Invisibility, Confusion. </span></div></li></ul><h2><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Actions</span></h2><hr/><ul><li><div><b><i>Multiattack.</i></b> The djinni makes three scimitar attacks.</div></li><li><div><b><i>Scimitar.</i></b> <i>Melee Weapon Attack:</i> +13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. <i>Hit: </i>(2d6 + 5) slashing damage plus (2d6)lightning or thunder damage. (djinni's choice)</div></li><li><div><b><i>Create Whirlwind.</i></b> A 5-foot-radius, 30-foot-tall cylinder of swirling air magically forms on a point the djinni can see within 120 feet of it. The whirlwind lasts as long as the djinni maintains concentration (as if concentrating on a spell). Any creature but the djinni that enters the whirlwind must succeed on a DC 20 Strength saving throw or be restrained by it. The djinni can move the whirlwind up to 60 feet as an action, and creatures restrained by the whirlwind move with it. The whirlwind ends if the djinni loses sight of it. A creature can use its action to free a creature restrained by the whirlwind, including itself, by succeeding on a DC 18 Strength check. If the check succeeds, the creature is no longer restrained and moves to the nearest space outside the whirlwind.</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b>MAYMUN - MARID Cleric 12 </b></div><ul><li><div><b>Init </b>+8;<b>Senses </b>Darkvision 60 Ft.;Perception +17</div></li><li><div><br/></div><h2><b>DEFENSE</b></h2></li><li><div><br/></div></li><li><div><b>AC </b>25, touch 14, flat-footed 18 (+4 Dex, +1 Dodge, +9 Natural, -1 Size)</div></li><li><div><b>hp 250 </b>(24d10+96)</div></li><li><div><b>Fort </b>+15, <b>Ref </b>+16, <b>Will </b>+13</div></li><li><div><br/></div></li><li><div><br/></div><h2><b>OFFENSE</b></h2></li><li><div><br/></div></li><li><div><b>Speed </b>20 ft., swim 60 ft.</div></li><li><div><b>Melee </b>2 Slams +21 (3d6+6) Or Mwk Trident +18/+13/+8 (3d6+9)</div></li><li><div><b>Special Attacks </b>Vortex (1/10 Minutes, 10-50 Ft. Tall, 1d8+4 Damage, Dc 22), Water Mastery, Water's Fury</div></li><li><div><b>Reach </b>10 ft.</div></li><li><div><b>Spell-Like Abilities </b>(CL 12; )</div><div style="padding-left:40px;">constant- detect evil, detect good, detect magic, water walk at will- create water, invisibility, plane shift (willing targets to elemental planes, astral plane, or material plane only), purify food and drink (liquids only), quench 5/day- control water, gaseous form, obscuring mist, water breathing 3/day- see invisibility 1/day- persistent image, cone of cold, wall of ice (dc 21) 1/year-grant 1 wish (to nongenies only</div></li><li><div><br/></div><h2><b>STATISTICS</b></h2></li><li><div><br/></div></li><li><div><b>Str </b>23, <b>Dex </b>19, <b>Con </b>18, <b>Int </b>14, <b>Wis </b>15, <b>Cha </b>16</div></li><li><div><b>Base Atk </b>+12; <b>CMB </b>19; <b>CMD </b>34</div></li><li><div><b>Feats </b>Combat Casting, Combat Reflexes, Dodge, Great Fortitude, Improved Initiative B, Improved Natural Attack, Power Attack,</div></li><li><div><b>Skills </b>Craft +17 Diplomacy +18 Knowledge (planes) +17 Perception +17 Sense Motive +17 Stealth +15 Swim +29</div></li><li><div><b>Languages </b>Aquan, Auran, Common, Ignan, Terran; Telepathy 100 Ft.</div></li><li><div><b>SQ </b>change shape (water elemental, humanoid or giant, alter self , elemental body iii , or giant form i )</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>#####</div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><h2><span style="color:rgb(13, 58, 153);--inversion-type-color:simple;">Al-Abyad, Dao Champion 12</span></h2><div><i>Large elemental, neutral evil</i></div><div><b>Armor Class</b> 24 (natural armor)</div><div><b>Hit Points</b> 387 (27d10 + 205) - 331</div><div><b>Speed</b> 30 ft., burrow 30 ft., fly 30 ft.</div><div><br/></div><div><b>STR </b>27 (+8)</div><div><b>DEX </b>12 (+1)</div><div><b>CON 26 (+8)</b></div><div><b>INT 12 (+1)</b></div><div><b>WIS 13 (+1)</b></div><div><b>CHA 14 (+2)</b></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Saving Throws</b> Int +8, Wis +12, Cha +9</div><div><b>Condition Immunities</b> <a href="https://5e.tools/conditionsdiseases.html#petrified_phb" rev="en_rl_none">petrified</a></div><div><b>Senses</b> <u>darkvision</u> 120 ft., passive Perception 11</div><div><b>Languages</b> Terran</div><div><b>Challenge</b> 11 (7,200 XP)</div><div><br/></div><div><b><i>Earth Glide.</i></b> The dao can burrow through nonmagical, unworked earth and stone. While doing so, the dao doesn't disturb the material it moves through.</div><div><br/></div><div><b><i>Elemental Demise.</i></b> If the dao dies, its body disintegrates into crystalline powder, leaving behind only equipment the dao was wearing or carrying.</div><div><br/></div><div><b><i>Innate Spellcasting.</i></b> The dao's innate spellcasting ability is Charisma (spell save DC 14, +6 to hit with spell attacks). It can innately cast the following spells, requiring no material components:</div><ul><li><div style="margin-bottom:3px;">At will: <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#detect%20evil%20and%20good_phb" rev="en_rl_none">detect evil and good</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#detect%20magic_phb" rev="en_rl_none">detect magic</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#stone%20shape_phb" rev="en_rl_none">stone shape</a></div></li><li><div style="margin-bottom:3px;">3/day each: <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#passwall_phb" rev="en_rl_none">passwall</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#move%20earth_phb" rev="en_rl_none">move earth</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#tongues_phb" rev="en_rl_none">tongues</a></div></li><li><div style="margin-bottom:3px;">1/day each: <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#conjure%20elemental_phb" rev="en_rl_none">conjure elemental</a> (earth elemental only), <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#gaseous%20form_phb" rev="en_rl_none">gaseous form</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#invisibility_phb" rev="en_rl_none">invisibility</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#phantasmal%20killer_phb" rev="en_rl_none">phantasmal killer</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#plane%20shift_phb" rev="en_rl_none">plane shift</a>, <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#wall%20of%20stone_phb" rev="en_rl_none">wall of stone</a></div></li></ul><div><b><i>Sure-Footed.</i></b> The dao has advantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws made against effects that would knock it <a href="https://5e.tools/conditionsdiseases.html#prone_phb" rev="en_rl_none">prone</a>.</div><div><br/></div><div>Actions</div><div><b><i>Multiattack.</i></b> The Dao makes two fist attacks or two maul attacks.</div><div><br/></div><div><b><i>Fist.</i></b> <i>Melee Weapon Attack:</i> +18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. <i>Hit:</i>  (4d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.</div><div><br/></div><div><b><i>Maul.</i></b> <i>Melee Weapon Attack:</i> +18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. <i>Hit:</i>  (6d6 + 12) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it must succeed on a DC 20 Strength check or be knocked <a href="https://5e.tools/conditionsdiseases.html#prone_phb" rev="en_rl_none">prone</a>.</div><div><br/></div><div><b>Variant: Genie Powers</b></div><div>Genies have a variety of magical capabilities, including spells. A few have even greater powers that allow them to alter their appearance or the nature of reality.</div><div><b><i>Disguises.</i></b> Some genies can veil themselves in illusion to pass as other similarly shaped creatures. Such genies can innately cast the <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#disguise%20self_phb" rev="en_rl_none">disguise self</a> spell at will, often with a longer duration than is normal for that spell. Mightier genies can cast the <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#true%20polymorph_phb" rev="en_rl_none">true polymorph</a> spell one to three times per day, possibly with a longer duration than normal. Such genies can change only their own shape, but a rare few can use the spell on other creatures and objects as well.</div><div><br/></div><div><b><i>Wishes.</i></b> The genie power to grant wishes is legendary among mortals. Only the most potent genies, such as those among the nobility, can do so. A particular genie that has this power can grant one to three wishes to a creature that isn't a genie. Once a genie has granted its limit of wishes, it can't grant wishes again for some amount of time (usually 1 year), and cosmic law dictates that the same genie can expend its limit of wishes on a specific creature only once in that creature's existence.</div><div>To be granted a wish, a creature within 60 feet of the genie states a desired effect to it. The genie can then cast the <a href="https://5e.tools/spells.html#wish_phb" rev="en_rl_none">wish</a> spell on the creature's behalf to bring about the effect. Depending on the genie's nature, the genie might try to pervert the intent of the wish by exploiting the wish's poor wording. The perversion of the wording is usually crafted to be to the genie's benefit.</div><div><br/></div><div>#####</div><div><br/></div><h1><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Al Ahmar - Efreeti Sorceror 12</span></b></h1><div style="text-align:start;"><i><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Large elemental, lawful evil</span></i></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Armor Class </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">20 (Natural Armor)</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Hit Points 290</span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);"> (28d10+112)</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Speed </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">40 ft., fly 60 ft.</span></div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">STR </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">22 (+6)</span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);"> </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">DEX </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">12 (+1)</span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);"> </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">CON </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">24 (+7)</span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);"> </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">INT </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">16 (+3)</span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);"> </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">WIS </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">15 (+2)</span></div><div><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);"> </span><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">CHA </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">16 (+3)</span></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Saving Throws </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Int +7, Wis +6, Cha +7</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Damage Immunities </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Fire</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Senses </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Darkvision 120 Ft., passive Perception 12</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Languages </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Ignan</span></div></li><li><div><b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Challenge </span></b><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">11 (7,200 XP)</span></div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;"><br/></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div><b><i><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Elemental Demise</span></i></b><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">. If the efreeti dies, its body disintegrates in a flash of fire and puff of smoke, leaving behind only equipment the djinni was wearing or carrying.</span></div></li><li><div><b><i><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Innate Spellcasting</span></i></b><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">. The efreeti's innate spell casting ability is Charisma (spell save DC 15, +7 to hit with spell attacks). It can innately cast the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: detect magic 3/day: enlarge/reduce, tongues 1/day each: conjure elemental (fire elemental only), gaseous form, invisibility, major image, plane shift, wall of fire</span></div></li></ul><h2><span style="color:rgb(88, 23, 13);">Actions</span></h2><hr/><ul><li><div><b><i>Multiattack.</i></b> The efreeti makes two scimitar attacks or uses its Hurl Flame twice.</div></li><li><div><b><i>Scimitar.</i></b> <i>Melee Weapon Attack:</i> +15 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. <i>Hit: </i>(3d6 + 6) slashing damage plus (3d6)fire damage.</div></li><li><div><b><i>Hurl Flame.</i></b> <i>Ranged Spell Attack:</i> +12 to hit, reach 120 ft., one target. <i>Hit: </i>(7d6) fire damage.</div></li></ul></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Best Cinematic ending to a campaign I&apos;ve ever had</title>
    <created>20210414T193710Z</created>
    <updated>20230906T224924Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Last night my latest Dungeons and Dragons campaign ended. It was perhaps the greatest cinematic ending I've ever run. </div><div><br/></div><div>We started with the party hurtling through the air in a the flying cauldron of Baba Yaga, crash landing in the middle of a battlefield with the Big Bad Evil Gal, The Raven Queen, slaughtering hundreds of innocents. The city of Ghealdar was flooded by a river, which was diverted by an earthquake caused by one of her minions. </div><div><br/></div><div>The party immediately began attacking her. They already proved to themselves they could beat her once. They were determined that this time she would not escape them at the end. The battle started off in terrifying fashion with the Raven Queen unleashing powerful magic spells that inflicted massive damage to the entire party - with the exception of the cleric, who had mysteriously disappeared. </div><div><br/></div><div>But the party immediately responded. Every member of the party contributed in a significant way. The fighters, Asher and Sadavir, immediately unleashed their greatest moves with sword and axe, inflicting massive damage and drew all of her attention. Draeven, the ranger, rained arrows on the entire battlefield, returning a barrage of damage that nearly incapacitated her minions. Before they died, the shadow elves minions piled on, dragging down Asher and knocking him unconscious. The wizard Cog, originally an animated suit of armor, now reforged into a legendary sword, struck the remaining minions down with a chain lightning spell. </div><div><br/></div><div>Meanwhile, in the ethereal realm, the cleric Briar was given a vision. She saw the souls of the Raven Queen's dead minions sacrificing their souls to keep her alive. She cast a spell that severed the connection between this being of ultimate evil, and the captive souls who didn't know how they had enslaved their eternal spirits. </div><div><br/></div><div>When Briar's spell struck, The Raven Queen realized what happened and immediately began begging for the thing she had been pursuing this entire time: the release of the elemental djinn from their gem prisons. She escaped the prison and sought to destroy the world to release them. She begged the party to release the djinn in return for her surrender and death. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>The Raven Queen stats</title>
    <created>20200929T172756Z</created>
    <updated>20210414T032617Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(4, 51, 255);">When trapped</span></span></span></b></div><ul><li><div style="text-align:start;">Etherealness (won't work with Shackes)</div></li><li><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Gaseous form</span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Raven's Call</span></span></span></div></li></ul><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(4, 51, 255);">Initial turn OOO: </span></span></span></b></div><ul><li><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">TURN 1 - meteor swarm + fear</span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">TURN 2 - Gaze attack at the biggest threat</span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">TURN 3 - Gaze attack at the biggest threat</span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">TURN 4 - Feeblemind casters</span></span></span></div></li><li><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">TURN 1 after taking damage: Time Stop: mirror image, blur, fear</span></span></span></div></li></ul><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The Raven Queen </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Medium Fey; Neutral Alignment; Goddess of Death </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Armor Class: 24 (Divine Aura) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Hit Points: 1,024 (80d20+224) - 351</span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Speed: 50 ft; 60 ft Flight </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Ability Scores </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Str: 16 Dex: 24 Con: 26 Int: 20 Wis: 22 Cha: 30 </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Saving Throws:</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> Str +10, Dex +16, Con +17, Int +14, Wis +15, Cha +19</span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Skills:</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> Insight +24, Perception +24, Stealth +25, Arcana +23, Nature +23, Religion +23</span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Damage Resistances:</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> Cold; Radiant </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Damage Immunities:</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> Necrotic; Poison; bludgeoning piercing and slashing that is nonmagical </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Senses</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">: Truesight 120 ft, passive perception 30 </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Languages</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> - All, telepathy 120 ft. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">CR</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">: 30 (155,000 EXP) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Features </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Multi-Spell.</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> Once per turn, the Raven Queen may opt to cast one spell with a casting time of one action as a bonus action. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Magic Resistance.</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> The Raven Queen has advantage on all saving throws caused by magical effects. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The Sands of Decay.</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> Any nonmagical equipment The Raven Queen holds is immediately aged until it turns to dust. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Legendary Resistance (3/Day).</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> When the Raven Queen would fail a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Actions </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Grasp.</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> Melee Weapon Attack: +13 to hit, Reach of 5 ft, One Target </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Hit: 11 (2d10) Necrotic Damage </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The Raven's Call. (1/Day)</span></span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">As an action, The Raven Queen calls to her followers to prove themselves worthy of her glory. In 1d4 turns, 1d6+2 Shadar-Kai Shadowdancers emerge from portals to the Shadowfell, appearing randomly in the area, up to the DM's discretion. If the Shadar-Kai are killed, The Raven Queen gains 40 temporary hit points for each defeated Shadowdancer. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Gaze.</span></span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The Raven Queen casts the gaze of Death itself upon one creature she can see. The target must succeed a DC 26 Wisdom saving throw or be subject to one of the following effects, determined randomly by rolling 1D6. 6s are a reroll. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">1. Gaze of Denial</span></span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The target is hit with the full emotional dread of the Shadowfell, and their mind finds it difficult to cope. The target suffers 3d8 Psychic damage and their Wisdom score is immediately reduced by 1d4. This effect can only be ended by a Greater Restoration or Wish spell. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">2. Gaze of Wrath</span></span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The target experiences an urge of defiance toward the encroachment of death. for the next 1d8 turns, the target receives 3d8 Necrotic damage at the start of each of their turns. If the target survives the final roll of this effect, they must make a Dexterity saving throw as they feel the earth beneath them begin to shake. On a failure, the target takes the total damage dealt by this ability as one blast of necrotic energy that erupts from the ground. On a success, they suffer no damage but are considered prone. Their turn then continues as normal. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">3. Gaze of Bargaining</span></span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The target is forced inward mentally. At the start of the target's next turn, they are given a proposition. They may choose not to act on this turn, or reduce their maximum HP by 40 and one of their ability scores (of their choice) by 2. If the target accepts the bargain, they awaken as their body begins to collapse and their turn proceeds as normal. If they do not accept this bargain, they are considered incapacitated until their next turn. When they awaken on their following turn, they are considered prone but suffer no other ill effects caused by this ability. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">4. Gaze of Depression</span></span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The target is flooded by emotion and are afflicted by a condition unique to this ability; Despair. Creatures afflicted by Despair cannot take reactions, and any actions or bonus actions taken require the target to pay a cost of 5 hit points. You cannot substitute temporary hit points for this cost. If the cost would reduce a creature's hit points to 0, the action is carried out as normal before the target falls unconscious. Any healing effect would cause the afflicted target to be healed and remain conscious. This effect can only be ended by a Greater Restoration or Wish spell. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">5. Gaze of Acceptance</span></span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">The target becomes infatuated with death, fascinated by it, and loses the will to resist it for 1d4 of its turns. During this time, the target cannot regain hit points by any means, and it has disadvantage on all saving throws caused by The Raven Queen or her allies. The target also gains a vulnerability to Necrotic damage for the duration. This effect can be ended early by a Greater Restoration or Wish spell. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Legendary Actions </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">At-Will Spell.</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> The Raven Queen casts one of her at-will spells. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Gaze.</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> (Costs 2 Actions) The Raven Queen can use her Gaze ability. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Teleport.</span></span></span></b><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);"> The Raven Queen casts Teleport. </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Spells </span></span></span></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Cantrips </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Chill Touch </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Prestidigitation </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">1st Level (At Will) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Sleep </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Hellish Rebuke </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Cure Wounds </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Detect Poison and Disease </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Command </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">2nd Level (At Will) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Knock </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Mirror Image </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Darkness </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Alter Self </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Silence </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Ray of Enfeeblement </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">3rd Level (At Will) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Counterspell </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Dispel Magic </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Fear </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Fireball </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Gaseous Form </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">4th Level (5 Slots) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Banishment </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Death Ward </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Dimension Door </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Blight </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">5th Level (5 Slots) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Greater Restoration </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Geas </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Scrying </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Flame Strike </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Insect Plague </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">6th Level (4 Slots) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Circle of Death </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Chain Lightning </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Flesh to Stone </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Heroes' Feast </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">7th Level (4 Slots) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Forcecage </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Finger of Death </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Delayed Blast Fireball </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Teleport </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Regenerate </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Etherealness </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Plane Shift </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">8th Level (3 Slots) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Feeblemind </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Dominate Monster </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Maze </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><hr/><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 22px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">9th Level (3 Slots) </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Meteor Swarm - reskinned as bubbles of evil</span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Power Word Kill </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">Time Stop </span></span></span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);margin-bottom:16px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="color:rgb(26, 26, 27);">True Resurrection </span></span></span></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 37</title>
    <created>20210331T000156Z</created>
    <updated>20210414T005946Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><b><u>The Second Battle of Ghealdar, or the Razing of Ghealdar, or the Flood of Ghealdar</u></b></div><div><br/></div><div>Banrion and Al-Abyad have diverted the Great River with a great earthquake, and Ghealdar is now underwater. The wealthy homes on the hill above the river are mostly fine, but the city is increasingly underwater to the South and East. The goblin Dump is completely submerged, and the goblins have fled North. </div><div><br/></div><div>The two Djinn are laying waste to the city. Al-Abyad is knocking down walls while Banrion attempts to unlock the Runegate in the town square. The town square where the orcs are encamped, with the runegate at the center, is a scene of slaughter and ruin, covered in 5-10 feet of water with dangerous rushing currents. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="color:rgb(24, 133, 226);">Briar sees full vision of the spirit realm in Ghealdar</span></b>. She sees swarms of elves swirling around Ghealdar, along with goblins and humans and orcs. </div><div><br/></div><div style="padding-left:40px;"><i>The heavens parted. I saw a seething mass of souls. The people of Ghealdar - humans, goblins, orcs and others - surrounded by the Tuatha De Danaan. The spirit disciples of the Raven Queen surrounded them, holding them down and preventing them from moving towards their eternal rest. </i></div><div style="padding-left:40px;"><i><span style="--en-markholder:true;"><br/></span></i></div><div style="padding-left:40px;"><i>I can see what I need to do. I will step into the realm of the grave, and fight for these souls. </i></div><div><br/></div><div>After some battle, <b><span style="color:rgb(24, 133, 226);">Banrion agrees to make a deal with the party</span></b>. She will allow herself to be captured again, if the party releases the rest of the Arch-Djinn. If not, she will disappear and haunt the realm forever. She will strike when nobody suspects, killing hundreds, and then disappear. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="color:rgb(24, 133, 226);">Tal'Aer will appear.</span></b> </div><div><br/></div><div style="padding-left:40px;"><i>"The Feywild is in shambles, much like this realm. Undead Fey spirits wander the land. Our people are returning to the mortal realm to do two things: reclaim our home, and reclaim our people." </i></div><div><br/></div><div>Baba Yaga will be the one to make the gem work with Tal'Aer's help, trapping The Raven Queen forever. </div><div><br/></div><div>All they have to do first is defeat Al-Abyad and take the djinn controlling gem from him, without killing him. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>The Arch-Dao took the gem that was embedded in the Staff of the Djinn. It has the ability to dominate djinn. </div><div><a href="evernote:///view/1617575/s15/2e324b5a-905a-ac20-e54b-95d73aa19235/b700018e-325e-48b9-dba0-a42d80e0b0b7/" rel="noopener noreferrer" rev="en_rl_none">The Great Djinn</a></div><div><br/></div><div>Each Djinn will have stories of how <b>Banrion Fitheach </b>led the Djinn when they were seeking refuge from the Celestials. </div><ul><li><div>Barqan (Air) - once upon a time, the Fey &amp; Mortal realms saw castles in the sky. The Celestials banished them to a new realm, now the Elemental Plane of Air. </div></li><li><div>Maymun (water) - there is no real reason for the Elemental Plane of Water to not intersect with the ocean, but the Celestials decided that the Kraken should only present in the Feywild. They used the Modrons to close the gap between the realms. </div></li><li><div>Al-Abyad (earth) - the longest-imprisoned djinn, now well and truly insane. The party may have no choice but to put him down. </div></li><li><div>Al-Ahmar (fire) - fire consumes excess fuel, creating new living space for new life. The plains have been the predominant part of Rune for centuries, but fires used to clear the plains. Now they grow and grow, and nothing has evolved or changed. The world of Domhaine an Duine needs to change or it will die when the fire comes. </div></li><li><div>Baba Yaga. The final creature caught in the crown is not a djinn, but a Fey. She is an archfey, and has been away from the Great Game for centuries. She will return to the Feywild and shake the Domhaine an Sidhe to its core. She will start by reclaiming the Saeserin Swamp. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><a href="https://www.5esrd.com/database/creature/baba-yaga/" rev="en_rl_none">https://www.5esrd.com/database/creature/baba-yaga/</a></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><ul><li><div>5 members of the Atanian nobility are using the gems to manufacture weapons</div></li><li><div>The King publicly orders everyone bring the gems to the Engineering school. </div></li><ul><li><div>The spymaster secretly relays additional orders: bring decoys to the school, bring the real gems to the King’s palace</div></li></ul><li><div>6 gems, each has a Djinn trapped inside of it. The Raven Queen was released from it? </div></li><li><div>The party needs to destroy the Djinn on their native planes (the Elemental Djinn)</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. He made the party promise to destroy the gem after destroying Banrion. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 36</title>
    <created>20210331T000156Z</created>
    <updated>20210331T002027Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>The Arch-Dao took the gem that was embedded in the Staff of the Djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen teleported to another plane to recover after the staff's retributive strike. </div><div><br/></div><div>Barachiel: release the djinn in their native elemental planes, and by the time you're done, they'll locate the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><a href="evernote:///view/1617575/s15/2e324b5a-905a-ac20-e54b-95d73aa19235/b700018e-325e-48b9-dba0-a42d80e0b0b7/" rel="noopener noreferrer" rev="en_rl_none">The Great Djinn</a></div><div><br/></div><div>Each Djinn will have stories of how <b>Banrion Fitheach </b>led the Djinn when they were seeking refuge from the Celestials. </div><ul><li><div>Barqan (Air) - once upon a time, the Fey &amp; Mortal realms saw castles in the sky. The Celestials banished them to a new realm, now the Elemental Plane of Air. </div></li><li><div>Maymun (water) - there is no real reason for the Elemental Plane of Water to not intersect with the ocean, but the Celestials decided that the Kraken should only present in the Feywild. They used the Modrons to close the gap between the realms. </div></li><li><div>Al-Abyad (earth) - the longest-imprisoned djinn, now well and truly insane. The party may have no choice but to put him down. </div></li><li><div>Al-Ahmar (fire) - fire consumes excess fuel, creating new living space for new life. The plains have been the predominant part of Rune for centuries, but fires used to clear the plains. Now they grow and grow, and nothing has evolved or changed. The world of Domhaine an Duine needs to change or it will die when the fire comes. </div></li><li><div>Baba Yaga. The final creature caught in the crown is not a djinn, but a Fey. She is an archfey, and has been away from the Great Game for centuries. She will return to the Feywild and shake the Domhaine an Sidhe to its core. She will start by reclaiming the Saeserin Swamp. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><a href="https://www.5esrd.com/database/creature/baba-yaga/">https://www.5esrd.com/database/creature/baba-yaga/</a> </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><ul><li><div>5 members of the Atanian nobility are using the gems to manufacture weapons</div></li><li><div>The King publicly orders everyone bring the gems to the Engineering school. </div></li><ul><li><div>The spymaster secretly relays additional orders: bring decoys to the school, bring the real gems to the King’s palace</div></li></ul><li><div>6 gems, each has a Djinn trapped inside of it. The Raven Queen was released from it? </div></li><li><div>The party needs to destroy the Djinn on their native planes (the Elemental Djinn)</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. He made the party promise to destroy the gem after destroying Banrion. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Rutherford&apos;s Mansion</title>
    <created>20190721T200133Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212406Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>The goblins are NOT doing ok. King Snuffy doesn’t like our new home. It turns out that Uncle Rutherford’s mansion is...in need of repairs. In fact, it might be beyond repair. </div><div><br/></div><div>Ok, yes, it’s beyond repair. </div><div><br/></div><div>But what am I supposed to do with it? </div><div><br/></div><div>The mansion has a giant, round hole in the middle of the ground floor, like the living room collapsed in a nearly perfect circle. Whatever caused that must have escaped by bursting through the front door. At least the roof is intact. </div><div><br/></div><div>I think it’s safe enough to sleep in, which is good because I spent most of my money getting here, thinking that I’d be inheriting more money. But the house has been neglected for so long that it looks like looters have picked over everything of value. I did find the secret door to the hidden chambers below. I’m not quite sure what they were meant for, but Uncle Rutherford kept an armory full of weapons. Most of those are rusted or corroded beyond repair. </div><div><br/></div><div>I did find a chamber that held broken eggshells. There were claw marks and corroded stone there, so I think that some sort of dragon lived there. But it seems unlikely that Uncle Rutherford would have kept a pet and then let it escape like that. </div><div><br/></div><div>There are also more tunnels beneath the basement, connected to the egg chamber. I haven’t wandered down those tunnels. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>I found something amazing the next day! I found an animated suit of armor. It talks and everything! I’m not sure what to do with it, or if I even own it. Can I own something that seems alive and sentient? </div><div><br/></div><div>King Snuffy says he doesn’t have a good feeling about this place, but I find it wonderfully interesting. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>The mansion is large. Two stories above ground. The ground floor holds a large kitchen, dining area, and drawing room. The second floor holds six bedrooms plus a massive master suite. There are three floors below ground. The first basement floor contains a grain, fruit and vegetable cellar and what looks like beds for servants. The second basement level contains an armory and even more spartan servant’s quarters. </div><div><br/></div><div>The third floor is protected by a large metal door and contains the rough-hewn egg chamber. </div><div><br/></div><div>The grounds around the mansion are wildly overgrown. It looks like there was a garden at one point, along with an orchard and hedges. It’s now grown into a wild mess that no gardener could untangle. Its possible that there are goblins or other creatures hiding in the grounds. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session One - 7/21/19</title>
    <created>20190721T202922Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212405Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>The party is gathered. </div><div><br/></div><div>Charlie’s character (NAME) and his family have been tasked with booting the squatters off of Tal’Eowan’s land near the Southeastern edge of Ghealdar’s state lands. </div><div><br/></div><div>Creatures included in the squatter band: (150 xp per encounter)</div><div><br/></div><div>Goblins</div><div>Goblin Inventor (as Kobold Inventor)</div><div>Illithid Thrall goblin</div><div>Quickling - Flit</div><div><br/></div><div>REWARDS</div><div><br/></div><div>In addition to XP, everyone who actually attends a session should get some sort of reward that is only available to those people. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>The Tuatha Dé Danaan</title>
    <created>20190810T164822Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212400Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div style="box-sizing: border-box; max-width: 100%; pointer-events: all;"><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; outline: none; font-size: 20px; pointer-events: none; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: pre-wrap; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 15px; color: rgb(33, 33, 33); font-family: Lato, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: none; font-weight: normal; line-height: 1.25;">The elves who have fought guerrilla warfare against Gibard saw an opportunity when Ghealdar’s economy collapsed and began attacking orcish business interests throughout Ghealdar. Nobody has been able to catch any members of the terrorist cell and their existence is without evidence.</span></h3></div><div>When Gibardan Orcs descended on the Hartland and swept the elves out of the forest, the elves thought they would be able to rely on Atania and the Aladdin from the Feywild city of Senaliesse. Unfortunately for Grandmaster Tarkin, Bladesinger Tal’Aer, and High Druidess Crysania, the leaders of the elves at the time, the Winter Queen was ascendant and prevented the Eladrin from mobilizing. Without the Eladrin, the newly reformed Atanian government and Engineering School decided that the danger was too much. </div><div><br/></div><div>It’s been 500 years. Tarkin is dead. Crysania is a crone living in the Feywild. Tal’Aer has disappeared. The next generation of elves took the Bladesingers’ training and transformed it. Their magic went from magic of war and beauty to deception and murder. </div><div><br/></div><div>The newly formed Tuatha Dé, with help and supplies from sympathetic members of the Engineering School and citizens of Senaliesse, began by attacking outposts around the borders of Gibard. They have repeatedly posted their demands throughout the nation of Gibard, on notices in Atania, and now they are showing up in Ghealdar.</div><div><br/></div><ol><li><div>The orcs belong in the mountains and not in the Hartland. They must withdraw and allow the elves to return. </div></li><li><div>Atania, Ghealdar and the other Free States must cease trade with Gibard</div></li><li><div>Gibard must pay reparations to the Tuathe Dé</div></li><li><div>Gibard must withdraw from Ghealdar</div></li></ol><div><br/></div><div>The leaders of the Tuatha Dé include unknown figures who all report to Crysania. They form individual cells that operate in small groups, unconnected from the others. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Bás Olphéist - Death to Orcs. An important leader in Ghealdar. His real name is Darragh. </div></li><li><div>Ag Fulaingt - Suffering. </div></li><li><div>Bua - Victory. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>These elves are all using the Shadowdancer rogue archetype. </div><div><br/></div><div>Silvermane’s CO: Captain Nurul. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 2 - 8/10/19</title>
    <created>20190810T015814Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212356Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>AWARDING INSPIRATION: advantage on any roll. </div><div><br/></div><div>I’d like to allow players to award inspiration for good roleplaying. Heroics, roleplaying. </div><div><br/></div><div>But every award of inspiration gives me an award for your foes. </div><div><br/></div><hr/><div><br/></div><div>Mercenaries in Isadorae’s mansion</div><div><br/></div><div>150 xp (6 bandits) + 450 (bandit captain who is a half-elf with a brother in Tuatha Dé). His name is Fenris, his terrorist brother’s name is Bás Olphéist (Death to Orcs). </div><div><br/></div><div>The Tuatha Dé are willing to meet, but only if the party does them a favor. They want: </div><ul><li><div>the head of an important orc</div></li><li><div>weaponry</div></li><li><div>support</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Cog</span>: How did Rutherford animate Cog? What other creatures or objects did he animate? What clues can I drop? Notes in a spellbook on Transmutation reference books that were hidden away in a vault in the Engineering School because creating life is too dangerous to explore. History/Occult check: a megalomaniacal wizard known as Cruthaigh (Creator) was the last one to actually do this. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">IF TIME</span>: Silvermane is requested back at Gibardan HQ. Reinforcements to deal with the dragon came in sooner than expected. A group of specialized dragon slayers have been hired by Tal’Aeowan. They appear very intimidating, but they are not capable of taking on this black dragon. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><en-media hash="c734fcf46e2739a9359247f12e1b5047" type="image/png" /><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><en-media hash="182faf59ce4ff82f72de0ef1ea4ada72" type="image/png" /><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>People at the bar: </div><ul><li><div>Notice how much money Cog has</div></li><li><div>Hears Isadorae talking about paying to have the house rebuilt</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>“That damn piece of junk” according to Cog was another, larger animated construct that could lift and repair things. </div><div><br/></div><div>There’s an Otyugh in the basement. There’s probably a small horde of them by now. </div><div><br/></div><div>Bennett &amp; Longshanks - two mercenaries who are friends with Draevan. </div><div><br/></div><div>The books in the mansion have been organized. Not filed the way Rutherford used to have them. Is it a code? They spell the words Victory. Suffering. Death to Orcs. The names of the Tuatha Dé in Ghealdar. </div><div><br/></div><div>Isadorae is sending a note to the Engineering School to ask about the message. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
