  <note>
    <title>Session 3 - 8/15/19</title>
    <created>20190812T033547Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212354Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>From previous session: the Tuatha will watch and wait to see what the party does, who they support, before they do any real outreach. </div><div><br/></div><div>Items leftover in the mansion: </div><ul><li><div>potion of healing</div></li><li><div>potion of greater healing</div></li><li><div>scroll of color spray</div></li><li><div>scroll of false life </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>_______</div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>The goblins start rioting. Torg and his minions come back to Ghealdar, accusing the orcs of kidnapping free goblins and torturing them. The goblins protest outside of the Orc encampment and things get out of control. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Tuatha Dé are providing material support and advice. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="border: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;"><font style="font-size: 18px;"><b>XP PER BATTLE (4 players): 900 HARD, 1600 DEADLY</b></font></span></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>STAGE 1 - RANDOM FIRES AND ATTACKS</div><div><br/></div><div>Fires are set in various places in the city. The city watch goes to investigate and something worse happens somewhere else. A valuable house is hit. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><i>Barghest: 1100 xp </i></b></div><div><b><i><br/></i></b></div><div><b><i>18 goblins + goblin boss = hard encounter</i></b></div><div><br/></div><div>STAGE 2 - THE ORCS RESPOND</div><div><br/></div><div>The orcs mobilize, pushing the goblins back into the slums. Just as it looks like things are going to settle down a handful of orcs get overzealous and slaughter a dozen goblins in front of witnesses. Those orcs are killed and/or rescued by the PC’s. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>6 Orcs + Orc Eye of Gruumsh</b></div><div><br/></div><div>STAGE 3 - FULL SCALE DISASTER </div><div><br/></div><div>Enraged, the goblins, supported by Tuatha archers, attack back, sweeping up the orcs, PCs, and others in mob violence. </div><div><br/></div><div><en-media hash="72a95f7fd81561999a3b7a7014e0e42a" type="image/png" /></div><div><br/></div><div>GOBLIN MOBS - become larger/more powerful at each stage of the riot</div><div><br/></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0.25em; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">Engulf: Being inside a mob of people should hurt. Kicking, biting, clawing, the more desperate the worse of the person will be. Maybe a str or dex save at the start of the turn to not eat some damage.
</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0.25em; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">Ranged: Most mobs will pick up rocks and hurl them at offending parties, but some might even make improvised grenades with molotovs.
</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">Melee: Multiattack actions are the way to go here. Lots of low damage attacks as the fringe of the mob lash out. Possibly even grappling and pulling people into the bulk of the mob to be torn at.
</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
