  <note>
    <title>The Industrialization &amp; Exportation of Magic in Atania</title>
    <created>20190826T161415Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212352Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>After the creation of industrialized magic in Atania, King Darian XIII made the decision to keep magical secrets close and not export magic en-masse. </div><div><br/></div><div>When it was discovered that the GURR was sneaking magic out of Atania one of the king’s ministers ordered a kingdom-wide inspection of loss-prevention methods and discovered that there was leakage across the kingdom. </div><div><br/></div><div>Atania has since created a program to legalize and regulate the export of magical production methods. There are experimental programs teaching some of the free states how to farm using the Ogham. The GURR is slowly being coaxed into unofficially working with the Atanian monarchy. </div><div><br/></div><div>While no means of production have yet been exported to Ghealdar, many industrialized magic items have been distributed to the goblins. A squadron of fireball-wand-wielding goblins are going to blow up the orcish line. </div><div><br/></div><div>One of the most groundbreaking wizards was experimenting with animating golems and suits of armor in a massive way, as well as trapping Outsiders as golems. An experiment he didn’t understand created a self-aware golem. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Cog</span>: How did Rutherford animate Cog? What other creatures or objects did he animate? What clues can I drop? Notes in a spellbook on Transmutation reference books that were hidden away in a vault in the Engineering School because creating life is too dangerous to explore. History/Occult check: a megalomaniacal wizard known as Cruthaigh (Creator) was the last one to actually do this. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 4 - 8/31/19</title>
    <created>20190820T041600Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212349Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>STAGE 2 - THE ORCS RESPOND</div><div><br/></div><div>Tur’og - Orcish commander </div><div><br/></div><div>The orcs mobilize, pushing the goblins back into the slums. Just as it looks like things are going to settle down a handful of orcs get overzealous and slaughter a dozen goblins in front of witnesses. Those orcs are killed and/or rescued by the PC’s. </div><div><br/></div><div>A squadron of ray of fire wand wielding goblins begins the counteroffensive by blowing up the line of orcs. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">6 Orcs + Orc Eye of Gruumsh (MM 247)</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Monster sets to use: 150 xp per player (750 xp) for a Medium encounter. </span>The first two encounters should be pretty easy. If they are, increase the number of monsters per encounter. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>12 orcs - 1200 xp</div></li><li><div>6 orcs, 6 blink dogs</div></li><li><div>Druid (orc), 3 orcs </div></li><li><div>Hobgoblin Devastator, 4 orcs - 850 xp </div></li><li><div>8 orcs with magical nets</div></li><li><div>Tuatha Dé Shadowdancer , 2 Meazel - this encounter is meant to kill at least one player so they can have an encounter with the Raven Queen. Probably Steve’s character. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>STAGE 3 - FULL SCALE DISASTER </div><div><br/></div><div>Enraged, the goblins, supported by Tuatha archers, attack back, sweeping up the orcs, PCs, and others in mob violence. </div><div><br/></div><div><en-media hash="72a95f7fd81561999a3b7a7014e0e42a" type="image/png" title="Attachment" /><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>GOBLIN MOBS - become larger/more powerful at each stage of the riot</div><div><br/></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0.25em; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">Engulf: Being inside a mob of people should hurt. Kicking, biting, clawing, the more desperate the worse of the person will be. Maybe a str or dex save at the start of the turn to not eat some damage.
</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0.25em; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">Ranged: Most mobs will pick up rocks and hurl them at offending parties, but some might even make improvised grenades with molotovs.
</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">Melee: Multiattack actions are the way to go here. Lots of low damage attacks as the fringe of the mob lash out. Possibly even grappling and pulling people into the bulk of the mob to be torn at.
</span></div><div style="text-align: center; padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-weight: bold;">####</span></span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">After the goblin horde makes its way out of The Dump, they destroy everything in their path for a mile or two. There’s a lull as the goblins riot and the party has an opportunity to speak to some of the goblins and convince them that the goblins are going to come back with massive reinforcements. Torg could be one of the goblins who emerges as a leader. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">The party can get them out via the underground chamber below Rutherford’s mansion. Cog knows this. This becomes a running battle to get as many goblins out as possible. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">The orcs murder them in droves. It’s a slaughter as the orcs call in reinforcements, but the goblin hordes break the orcs and the city descends into riots for a day or two, until the orcs open the Runegates to transport more reinforcements. The new reinforcements include war wizards, who slaughter goblins. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">The opening of the Runegate means they travel through the Feywild, and some Unseelie Fey creatures come along for the ride. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">At the same time, Torg and his minions have come to the city to figure out who killed the dragon wyrmlings. After the party unloads or sells the dragon parts Torg’s minions come calling. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">The party needs to be sent on a quest to get away from Torg. Something about Elemental Myrmidons sent by the creator of Cog. A rogue fey sorcerer. </span></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
