  <note>
    <title>Party Breakdown</title>
    <created>20190714T034411Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212347Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Party Breakdown</div><ul><li><div>Chris - Isadorae the Gnome, niece to Rutherford, heir to his estate. Wizard/summoner class. Nicknamed “Dullteeth” by the Engineers Guild. Connected to the story as the owner of an estate where mercenaries hang out. </div></li><li><div>Steve - Rheada half-elf mapmaker. Hired by Charlie’s character to show the borders of Tal’Aeowan’s land. </div></li><li><div>Nicholas - Silvermane, an orc paladin who is trying to enforce the law. </div></li><li><div>Charlie - Asher Human noble, scion of an influential Ghealdarian family. Hired to start the adventure. </div></li><li><div>Brian - Cog. An animated suit of armor with no memories. He woke up in Rutherford’s mansion. </div></li><li><div>Adam - Draevan, a half-orc, half-elf fighter. Living at Rutherford’s mansion. </div></li><li><div>Evan - Sadavir Blessedarmor, dwarven barbarian, kin slayer and escapee from the dwarven kingdom. Also living at Rutherford’s mansion. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><font style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">Chris Beatty</span></font></div><div><br/></div><div>Everyone should look neat and tidy, and everything should be put in its place. The Wizards and Sages at the School of Arcana in Atania have given me a home for the past 200 years, and it is my job to keep its towers organized. I turn in my keys every evening, and I am allowed two meals a day. The work isn't exactly fulfilling, but being around such creative and brilliant minds is worth it. The Goblins have accepted me as one of their own, and I'm pretty content with that. After a decade, I was given the name "Dullteeth", and I wear it like a badge of honor. Years ago I heard rumors about Goblin slaves, and then Goblin liberation in the free-state of Ghaeldar, but what came of that, I'm unsure. I think I had a relative near there at one point; a second cousin, twice removed? He was apparently quite rich and dealt in rare artifacts. He isn't an honorary Goblin like me, but I won't hold that against him.</div><div><br/></div><div>While cleaning a former high-wizard's quarters I found a book hidden under his bed - This room hadn't had anyone use it in decades, so this book was obviously not precious, and it was covered with a very large layer of dust, so I took it. It needed cleaning and a bit of reconditioning as some of the pages had some water damage! Really! It was a very pretty blue color and had a strange marking on the front of it that I think I recognized from other books and on various doors of the School. Taking it to my quarters, I found that I could read every fifth or sixth word written in it? So I did what any aspiring wizard would do: I tried to cast this ritual. I tried and tried for weeks and weeks with little to no success.. But on one fateful evening I said what I think were the right words, and everything went black for a moment: after, my mind was filled with strange sensations all over my body, and I could see and hear the sounds of my chambers, but from much higher up. I saw myself lying on the floor, motionless, and I thought "OH NO, I'VE TURNED INTO A WALL" and started to cry. </div><div><br/></div><div>A few more moments pass and I came back to my senses and I see this hulking.. Thing.. In front of me. He had one arm like a grizzly bear but with blue fur and massive talons, another that looked like a tentacle. It walked on two uneven legs, and looked like it was dirty laundry sewn together over the form of a 50 different animals. I blacked out, and woke up a few hours later. I woke to it still standing there, kinda dumbfounded. Swaying back and forth slightly. One of its fingers seemed a little loose, and it was trying to push it back on.</div><div><br/></div><div>I don't know what it is, but I call him King Snuffy as he wears a crown and sometimes his nose is runny. He helps me when no one else is around, and we talk occasionally, though he doesn't seem to have much to say.</div><div><br/></div><div>--</div><div><br/></div><div>One evening I receive a letter saying that I do, indeed, have a distant relative. Or I did. And he does live in Ghaeldar. Or he did. And that I'm set to receive some of his money when he dies. Which he has. So I told my employers, and I am leaving my home. King Snuffy and I are going to take a boat! On the water! And see things like sand! It's terribly exciting. I hope the other Goblins in this free city are doing okay! </div><div><br/></div><div><font style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">Steve Grawrock</span></font></div><div><br/></div><div>I understand why you’ve come to me. A world famous cartographer does seem like the type to approach about ascertaining the political boundaries of Ghealdar to provide legitimate claims to your peace keeping forces. What I’m afraid will happen, however, is that this specific job will not involve just danger, but perhaps out and out warfare. On the matter, while I am quite neutral on the occupation of Tuatha Da Danaan, my distant kin may not see the complex nature of political allegiances if they were to find me amongst your gathering of ‘professionals’. </div><div><br/></div><div>All this being said, I feel compelled to do it. The chance to verify the extent of Ghealdar’s borders is exciting. To corroborate this verification it would be important to also study the original claims to land and ownership of the kingdom. Without access to these papers, it would be of little use to bring someone, such as myself, into this mission in the first place. If I am able to study these papers, I would be willing to join this peacekeeping mission. The usual monetary compensation will also be required. Thank you.</div><div><br/></div><div>-Rhaeadar Faeluck</div><div><br/></div><div>Bronwyn Faeluck, the wood elf, began his travels penniless and destitute. He left with a hope for something else, and found it. Stumbling into the faewilds, Bronwyn was brought before the court of Vulparia Moonpearl. She was entertained by his desperate pleas for help and offered a pact. Which he took, his family would have wealth, and success, but owe the best treasures, the best rare items to Vulparia herself. In what seemed to be a win win situation, he took it.</div><div><br/></div><div>However, conflicts in the Fae courts run deep, and Bronwyn met an early demise from the hands of Fae assassins. No one besides family, learned of the pact. Bronwyn’s daughter was next to hold the pact, Jandriel. Jandriel also expanded on the Faeluck name, bringing more fame and renown. In front of of Rhaeadar, Jandriel was killed by two assassins of a competing court. There was a warning given to him, break the pact, or face the same fate. </div><div><br/></div><div>After seeing the rock Rhaeadar was put under, he was about to meet the hard place he would be stuck in between. Vulparia made certain that he understood his place in the pact, and the long span his family still owed to her.</div><div><br/></div><div>Rhaeadar continued exploring, searching for more rare artifacts, mapping his progress and studying the creatures he ran in to, continually keeping a watch over his back, making sure assassins weren’t there to put a knife in it.</div><div><br/></div><div>He accepted the call to help the marauding elves, but is wary of their attitude towards a wood elf working for the orcish peace keepers. He also wants to be able to study the records of the Ghealdar city to see the original boundary lines.</div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 5 - 9/20/19</title>
    <created>20190820T041600Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212344Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>STAGE 2 - THE ORCS RESPOND</div><div><br/></div><div>Tur’og - Orcish commander gave Silvermane leave to rest. As the party is leaving, they see Draevan leading a group of goblins to safety. They are being chased by orcish soldiers and the party has to choose whether or not to help him and the goblins. Does Silvermane become an open traitor, killing all witnesses, or does he do something else? </div><div><br/></div><div>The party is running low on resources. They can’t handle a boss-level fight right now. Keep the pressure on them with lots of small fights. </div><div><br/></div><div>The orcish occupation force grows to more than 10,000, in ranks with dozens of war wizards (Hobgoblin Devastators)</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Monster sets to use: 150 xp per player (750 xp) for a Medium encounter. </span>The first two encounters should be pretty easy. If they are, increase the number of monsters per encounter. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>12 orcs - 1200 xp</div></li><li><div>6 orcs, 6 blink dogs</div></li><li><div>Druid (orc), 3 orcs </div></li><li><div>Hobgoblin Devastator, 4 orcs - 850 xp </div></li><li><div>8 orcs with magical nets</div></li><li><div>Tuatha Dé Shadowdancer , 2 Meazel - this encounter is meant to kill at least one player so they can have an encounter with the Raven Queen. Probably Steve’s character. </div></li><li><div>6 Orcs + Orc Eye of Gruumsh (MM 247)</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">STAGE 4 - FULL SCALE DISASTER </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">The orcs murder goblins in droves. It’s a slaughter as the orcs call in reinforcements. The new reinforcements include war wizards, who lay waste to the goblins with spells. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; border: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">The opening of the Runegate means they travel through the Feywild, and some Unseelie Fey creatures come along for the ride. An agent of the Raven Queen who helps the Tuatha Dé and </span><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-weight: bold;">Syrpha</span><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; border: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">, an agent of </span><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-weight: bold;">Vulparia the Archfey</span><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; border: 0px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(26, 26, 27); font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;-en-paragraph:true;">At the same time, Torg and his minions have come to the city to figure out who killed the dragon wyrmlings. After the party unloads or sells the dragon parts Torg’s minions come calling. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">The party needs to be sent on a quest to get away from Torg. Something about Elemental Myrmidons sent by the creator of Cog, a rogue fey sorcerer. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;"><span style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold;">MAGIC ITEM FOR RHAEDA TO GIVE TO HIS PATRON</span></span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">Carried by an Orc Devastator or another creature the party kills. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">It was forged by a gnome tinker wizard, but was improved and altered by Tal’Aer. It’s a magical key to a chamber that he uses to store magic items. He ostensibly lost it, but placed it so that it would come back to him and lead him to have a chance to help whoever returns it become aware of the Raven Queen. The item is metamorphic. </span><span style="font-size: 14px;">Ring of Free Action (Arcanist attunement only). </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">Vulparia Moonpearl is an Archfey, but just barely. She’s not anywhere near as powerful as the senior Court, and can’t hope to touch the Raven Queen. When Rhaeda is approached by an agent of Vulparia, the Raven Queen will pounce, sending the Tuatha Dé after the party. </span><span style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold;">Syrpha</span><span style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">, lvl 6 </span>Sorcerer, and Apitox, Nimblewright construct, come to collect the item from Rhaeda. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 6 - 10/19/19</title>
    <created>20191016T011308Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212342Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">Daily encounter budget: 10,200 xp</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">Medium encounter: 1500 xp</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">MAGIC ITEM FOR RHAEDA TO GIVE TO HIS PATRON</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">Carried by an Orc Devastator or another creature the party kills. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">It was forged by a gnome tinker wizard, but was improved and altered by Tal’Aer. It’s a magical key to a chamber that he uses to store magic items. He ostensibly lost it, but placed it so that it would come back to him and lead him to have a chance to help whoever returns it become aware of the Raven Queen. The item is metamorphic. </span><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">Ring of Free Action (Arcanist attunement only). </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">Vulparia Moonpearl is an Archfey, but just barely. She’s not anywhere near as powerful as the senior Court, and can’t hope to touch the Raven Queen. When Rhaeda is approached by an agent of Vulparia, the Raven Queen will pounce, sending the Tuatha Dé after the party. </span><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold;">Syrpha</span><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">, lvl 6 </span><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">Sorcerer, and Apitox, Nimblewright construct, come to collect the item from Rhaeda. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><b>Zel, the Dragon,</b> is under the influence of the Raven Queen. He succumbed to her influence in order to be able to lay waste to the Orcs. He killed thousands of them before being driven off, barely surviving. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><b>Rhaeda</b> will be given an opportunity to have her fey bond transferred to the Raven Queen, setting up the party to be attacked by Syrfa, the Succubus Fey. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">SAESARIN SWAMP</span></span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">In the swamp, the party is seeking out The Raven Queen to get help with ? </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">Set up an encounter between Silvermane and his patron. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Cruthaigh, Cog’s creator shows up to reclaim ownership of Cog, and the party might need to protect him. The wizard’s minions attack the party but gets attacked by the Raven Queen. </div><ul><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Pentadrone (MM 227), 450 xp</div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Flesh Golem (MM 170), 1800 xp</div></li></ul><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">The party makes its way through the swamp, occasionally running into more Shadowdancing Tuatha De, then encounters the Fairie Dragon realm. This is a section of the Jungle where the fairy dragons have always lived. They are the cousins of an Ancient Black Dragon that goes by Charbidis. If the party kills them, Charbidis will come after them. If they don’t kill them, then Charbidis will help them and explain that his cousin, Zel'terranon, has fallen under the sway of the Raven Queen. </div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Charbidis will also explain that the Lizardfolk used to worship him as a god, but since the Raven Queen showed up their loyalties have shifted. If the party can get the Lizardfolk to shift their allegiances back, he will help them. </div><ul><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Fairie Dragons (one of each color, 2100 xp), Lizard folk shaman x2</div></li><ul><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Dangerous terrain hidden by illusions: quicksand, pit traps, hidden trees that characters run into. Snares. </div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">The Fairie dragons </div></li></ul><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Lizardfolk King (1100 xp), Shaman (450), Lizardfolk (100). </div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Tuatha Dé Shadowdancer (2)</div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">A hag that impersonates the Raven Queen!! An entire coven that impersonates lizard folk and created a following for themselves, sowing chaos between them, the halflings, and the Raven Queen followers. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Rhaeda’s familiar sneaks into the shaman’s house, who is not there. </div><div><br/></div><div>A Lizardfolk named Zerit sneaks out to tell the party that lizardfolk are disappearing and he thinks the Shaman is responsible. Can they help? Zerit will tell them where to find the shaman at night, which will be a trap laid by Zerit. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Syrpha, Succubus Fey Sorceror, servant of Vulparia Moonpearl</title>
    <created>20191107T000531Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212340Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><font style="font-size: 14px;">When on a killing mission, Syrpha will bring 1 - 5 Unseelie minions with her as support. <br/></font></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left; color: rgb(85, 85, 85); font-family: Lato, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; zoom: 1; overflow: hidden;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; zoom: 1; overflow: hidden; vertical-align: top;"><h3 style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: inherit; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 24px;"></h3><h3><span style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(45, 18, 71);">Syrpha, Servant of Vulparia</span></h3><h3><br/></h3><h3><span style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(153, 153, 153); font-size: 15.6px; line-height: 1;">Female Mysterious Fey, any alignment</span></h3></div></div><hr style="box-sizing: content-box; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-right-style: initial; border-bottom-style: initial; border-left-style: initial; border-right-color: initial; border-bottom-color: initial; border-left-color: initial; border-image: initial; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: rgb(238, 238, 238); background: rgb(45, 18, 71);" /><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Armor Class: </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">13 (with mage armor)</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Hit Points: </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">33 (6d8 +6)</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Speed: </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">30ft (9m / 6 sqr)</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Proficiency: </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">+3</span></div><hr style="box-sizing: content-box; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-right-style: initial; border-bottom-style: initial; border-left-style: initial; border-right-color: initial; border-bottom-color: initial; border-left-color: initial; border-image: initial; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: rgb(238, 238, 238); background: rgb(45, 18, 71);" /><div style="box-sizing: border-box; text-align: center;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">STR</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">7 (-2)
</span></div></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">DEX</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">11 (+0)
</span></div></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">CON</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">13 (+1)
</span></div></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">INT</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">10 (+0)
</span></div></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">WIS</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">8 (-1)
</span></div></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">CHA</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">15 (+2)
</span></div></div></div><hr style="box-sizing: content-box; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-right-style: initial; border-bottom-style: initial; border-left-style: initial; border-right-color: initial; border-bottom-color: initial; border-left-color: initial; border-image: initial; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: rgb(238, 238, 238); background: rgb(45, 18, 71);" /><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(45, 18, 71); font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Challenge:</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(45, 18, 71);-en-paragraph:true;"> 3 (700 XP)</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(45, 18, 71);-en-paragraph:true;"> </span></div><hr style="box-sizing: content-box; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-right-style: initial; border-bottom-style: initial; border-left-style: initial; border-right-color: initial; border-bottom-color: initial; border-left-color: initial; border-image: initial; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: rgb(238, 238, 238); background: rgb(45, 18, 71);" /><h4 style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 18px;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 18px;">Actions
</span></h4><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Quarterstaff.</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">Melee Weapon Attack</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;"> +1 to hit, reach 5 ft, one target. Hit: 1 (1d6 -2 ) bludgeoning damage.</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 10px; font-style: italic; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 10px; font-style: italic;-en-paragraph:true;">Properties: Versatile (1d8),
</span></div><hr style="box-sizing: content-box; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-right-style: initial; border-bottom-style: initial; border-left-style: initial; border-right-color: initial; border-bottom-color: initial; border-left-color: initial; border-image: initial; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: rgb(238, 238, 238); background: rgb(45, 18, 71);" /><h4 style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 18px;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(45, 18, 71); font-size: 18px;">Spells</span></h4><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Spellcasting.</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;"> the Evoker is an 6th-level sorcerer. Its spellcasting ability is Charisma (spell save DC 13, to hit with spell attacks +5)</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">Cantrips (at will): </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">Message, Fire Bolt, Acid Splash, Mending,</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">1st level (4 slots):</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">Silent Image, Detect Magic, Ray of Sickness, Fog Cloud, Sleep, Shield, Mage Armor,</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">2nd level (3 slots):</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">Cloud of Daggers, Hold Person, Scorching Ray,</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">3rd level (3 slots):</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;"> </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">Dispel Magic,</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><a href="http://hardcodex.ru/" style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(45, 18, 71);-en-paragraph:true;"> Click here to see spells descriptions (external tool)</a></div><hr style="box-sizing: content-box; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-right-style: initial; border-bottom-style: initial; border-left-style: initial; border-right-color: initial; border-bottom-color: initial; border-left-color: initial; border-image: initial; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: rgb(238, 238, 238); background: rgb(45, 18, 71);" /><h4 style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 18px;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(45, 18, 71); font-size: 18px;">Special Abilities</span></h4><div><span style="font-weight: bold; box-sizing: border-box;">Elemental Bending: </span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;">When casting a area spell that deals fire, ice, lighting or thunder damage the evoker can exclude a number of targets from its area equal to its spellcasting modifier. The target dont receive any damage or effect from that spell.</span></div><div><br/></div><hr style="box-sizing: content-box; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-right-style: initial; border-bottom-style: initial; border-left-style: initial; border-right-color: initial; border-bottom-color: initial; border-left-color: initial; border-image: initial; border-top-style: solid; border-top-color: rgb(238, 238, 238); background: rgb(45, 18, 71);" /><h4 style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 18px;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 18px;">Racial Features
</span></h4><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Ability Modifiers</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">: +2 Cha, +1 Int
</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Hellish Resistance</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">: You have resistance to fire damage
</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Darkvision</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">: 60ft (18m / 12sqr)
</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Fey Legacy</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">: You know the Command cantrip. If your CR is 3 once per day you can cast Command and you can cast Darkness once per day. Charisma as spellcasting ability for those spells.
</span></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">Languages</span><span style="box-sizing: border-box;-en-paragraph:true;">: speaks Common and Fey
</span></div></div><div style="box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 1px; padding-left: 15px; padding-right: 15px; float: left; color: rgb(85, 85, 85); font-family: Lato, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><br/></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><font style="font-size: 24px;"><b>Apitox</b></font></span></div><div><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div style="text-align: center; border-radius: 3px 3px 0px 0px; overflow: hidden; color: rgb(68, 68, 68); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, HelveticaNeue, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div style="padding: 0px; vertical-align: middle;"><a href="https://thirdtofifth.tumblr.com/image/173268250019"><en-media hash="71bf88fc8558e107020730b5e0fa9110" type="image/png" width="464" /></a></div></div><p style="line-height: 1.6;"></p><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Nimblewright</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;">Medium construct, unaligned</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Armor Class</span> 19 (natural armor)</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Hit Points </span>127 (15d8 + 60)</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Speed </span>40 ft.</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Str</span> 19, <span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Dex</span> 24, <span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Con</span> 19, <span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Int</span> 10, <span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Wis</span> 17, <span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Cha</span> 19</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Damage Immunities</span> poison</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Damage Vulnerabilities</span> cold</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Condition Immunities</span> charmed, exhaustion, frightened, petrified, poisoned, stunned</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Senses </span>darkvision 60 ft. passive Perception 13</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Languages </span>Common, Dwarvish, Elvish</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Challenge </span>7 (2900 XP)</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Magic Resistance.</span> The nimblewright has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Superior Critical.</span> The nimblewright’s rapier attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 18-20.</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Actions</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;">Multiattack.</span> The nimblewright makes two melee attacks.</div><div><br/></div><div style="margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.6;-en-paragraph:true;">Rapier. </span><span style="font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;-en-paragraph:true;">Melee Weapon Attack:</span><span style="-en-paragraph:true;"> +10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. </span><span style="font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;-en-paragraph:true;">Hit:</span><span style="-en-paragraph:true;"> 14 (2d6+7) slashing damage. On a critical hit, the target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw, or fall prone.
</span></div><p></p><div style="line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="line-height: 1.6;-en-paragraph:true;">Animated by the spirit of a water elemental, the nimblewright’s ancestry is reflected in its fluid movements. These elite constructs are sometimes used as assassins. Fiendishly quick with their dual rapiers, nimblewrights spin about in a whirlwind of violence. Being intelligent, they also can serve as spies, disguising themselves as humanoids in order to do so. Despite a slight tinny quality to their voices, they are more than capable of appearing human at first glance, and even further interaction. 
</span></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
