  <note>
    <title>Session 7</title>
    <created>20191021T170510Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212335Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="font-size: 14px; orphans: 2; widows: 2;">The party wants to head to the Black City and recon. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; orphans: 2; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="orphans: 2; widows: 2;">"You don’t want a </span>family.”</div><div><br/></div><div>Draevan &amp; Silvermane are half-brothers. </div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; orphans: 2; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; orphans: 2; widows: 2;">####</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; orphans: 2; widows: 2;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; orphans: 2; widows: 2;">Daily encounter budget: 10,200 xp</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);-en-paragraph:true;">Medium encounter: 1500 xp</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-weight: bold;-en-paragraph:true;">MAGIC ITEM FOR RHAEDA TO GIVE TO HIS PATRON</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">Carried by a lizard folk King or similar creature. </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: normal;orphans: 2;text-indent: 0px;text-transform: none;white-space: normal;widows: 2;word-spacing: 0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;-en-paragraph:true;">It was forged by a gnome tinker wizard, but was improved and altered by Tal’Aer. It’s a magical key to a chamber that he uses to store magic items. He ostensibly lost it, but placed it so that it would come back to him and lead him to have a chance to help whoever returns it become aware of the Raven Queen. The item is metamorphic, it can change shape and features. </span><span style="border: 0px; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold;">Ring of Free Action</span> (Arcanist attunement only). </span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">Vulparia Moonpearl is an Archfey, but just barely. She’s not anywhere near as powerful as the senior Court, and can’t hope to touch the Raven Queen. When Rhaeda is approached by an agent of Vulparia, the Raven Queen will pounce, sending the Tuatha Dé after the party. </span><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold;">Syrpha</span><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;">, lvl 6 </span><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">Sorcerer, and Apitox, Nimblewright construct, come to collect the item from Rhaeda. </span><a href="evernote:///view/1617575/s15/ea62d9d9-5dbe-49cb-a509-11409c45fd2a/ea62d9d9-5dbe-49cb-a509-11409c45fd2a/" style="color: rgb(105, 170, 53);">Syrpha, Succubus Fey Sorceror, servant of Vulparia Moonpearl</a> </div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">TREASURE IN THE LIZARDFOLK LAIR</span></span></div><ul><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">Scroll: Mass Healing Word</span></div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Potion of Invulnerability</div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">2 Potions of Greater Healing</div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">2 Javelins +1</div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Bag of Beans</div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Brooch of Shielding</div></li></ul><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; font-weight: bold;">SAESARIN SWAMP</span></div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold;">Charbidis</span> will also explain that the Lizardfolk used to worship him as a god, but since the Raven Queen showed up their loyalties have shifted. If the party can get the Lizardfolk to shift their allegiances back, he will help them. </div><div style="text-align: start;">The Lizardfolk Zerit is actually a Night Hag who has tricked the Lizardfolk village into believing that the party is sent by the black dragon Charbidis. They have agreed to murder the party so that Charbidis knows the power of the Raven Queen. </div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">The Hag knows what the Raven Queen looks like because she saw her in her own dreams and vowed to work for her, but broke that vow. </div><ul><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">Lizardfolk King (1100 xp), Shaman (450), Lizardfolk (100). </span></div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">Tuatha Dé Shadowdancer (2)</span></div></li><li><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;"><span style="border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2;">A hag that impersonates the Raven Queen!! An entire coven that impersonates lizard folk and created a following for themselves, sowing chaos between them, the halflings, and the Raven Queen followers. </span></div></li></ul><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">Zerit, or the Night Hag Sora Kell, will flee if she is reduced below half HP. She will then begin stalking the party to bring them down. </div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">AFTER THE LIZARDFOLK</div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">If the party kills Sora Kell/Zerit, they can turn the Lizardfolk back to Charbidis. If they bring the Lizardfolk to Charbidis, he will eat one of them as a sacrifice. He will also tell the party more about the Black City and the Raven Queen. </div><div style="padding: 0.8em 0px 0px; border: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; widows: 2; margin-top: 1em; margin-bottom: 1em;">                <span style="font-style: italic;">The oldest of our kind do not know the full story of the Raven Queen. </span><span style="font-style: italic;">She is a being beyond your mortal comprehension. Cast out of the Feywild before Seelie or Unseelie. She was thrust into the Shadow Realm, but somehow she is here. She has built a city whose blackness has become the beating heart of the Saeserin. Her song emanates from the Black City. I suggest you run before you hear it, mortals. Her song that calls to the newly dead cannot be unheard once its heeded. Even my fellow wyrms are subject to her charms. My cousin, perhaps you know him, Zel’kenneroth? He hears her song and has become her missionary among the young wyrms. So run. Run away and live the rest of your pitiable lives in obscurity, and pray to your Creator that you do not heed the song of the Raven Queen. </span></div><div><br/></div><div>IDEA: </div><div><br/></div><div>Greater Behirs as enemies of the dragons in the near future. <a href="https://i.redd.it/bvpfccqlri331.png">https://i.redd.it/bvpfccqlri331.png</a> </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 8</title>
    <created>20191111T180953Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212333Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>As the party leaves the site of the recent battle with Vulparia’s agents, they must find their way to the Black City. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">ISADORAE CORRUPTED </span></div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen tempts away Isadorae, and Chris’ new character appears. WHAT WOULD TEMPT HER?</div><div><br/></div><div>King Snuffy will be the new Oath of Conquest paladin. His Paladin patron is an archfey who is opposed to the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>When the party heads toward the Black City, other beings take notice. Valparia lets things slip in a drunken whining session in the Winter Court. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">THE PALADIN CALLINGS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel, the Hamadryad de facto ruler of Cendriane, appears in the swamp, alongside Cassandra, the elven high priestess of the Spirits.</div><div><br/></div><div>In addition, the Creator inspires a group of halfling paladins and clerics to make a foray into the jungle. They arrive just as Tinuviel, Cassandra appear. The leader of the halflings is a cleric named <span style="font-weight: bold;">Amergin</span>. She and the other members of the party ride trained pigs into battle. The party hears him singing this song. </div><div><br/></div><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">"I am the wind on the sea;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am the wave of the sea;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am the bull of seven battles;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am the eagle on the rock
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am a flash from the sun;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am the most beautiful of plants;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am a strong wild boar;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am a salmon in the water;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am a lake in the plain;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am the word of knowledge;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am the head of the spear in battle;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I am the god that puts fire in the head;
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">Who spreads light in the gathering on the hills?
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">Who can tell the ages of the moon?
</span></dd><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">Who can tell the place where the sun rests?"</span><sup style="unicode-bidi: isolate; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 11.2px;"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amergin_Gl%C3%BAingel#cite_note-3" style="background-image: none; font-size: 11.2px; vertical-align: super; color: rgb(11, 0, 128); font-family: sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: 1; text-decoration: none;">[3]</a></sup></dd><div><br/></div><div>When all of them are gathered, the party learns that the great powers of the world have awakened to the reality of the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">SYRPHA COMES</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Vulparia sends a boon for Rhaeda, giving him a rough map of the Black City approach. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">THE APPROACH TO THE BLACK CITY</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tupelo trees in five feet of water surround the approaches to the Black City. The only land route to the city is hidden and guarded by the Raven Queen’s minions. Otherwise boats and swimming are required. </div><div><br/></div><div>On the main road, the party will meet <span style="font-weight: bold;">Tuatha De Shadowdancers. </span></div><div><br/></div><div>To the West of the main road there is <span style="font-weight: bold;">a tribe of trolls and ettins</span>. They have resisted the Raven Queen’s calls, and are annoyed by any small races approaching the city. </div><div><br/></div><div>To the East of the road lies the territory of a horrific <span style="font-weight: bold;">hydra</span>. There are sentient plants throughout the area. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 9</title>
    <created>20191204T232749Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212331Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Shadar-Kai (Shadowdancer) tactics post: <a href="http://themonstersknow.com/shadar-kai-tactics/">http://themonstersknow.com/shadar-kai-tactics/</a> </div><div><br/></div><div>PARTY NEEDS MAGIC ITEMS    </div><div><br/></div><div>In the Hydra Lair: </div><ul><li><div>Potion of Climbing</div></li><li><div>Potion of Clairvoyance x 2</div></li><li><div>Oil of Etherealness</div></li><li><div>Oil of Sharpness</div></li><li><div>Spell scroll (1st level) Gust</div></li><li><div>Spell scroll (6th) Conjure Fey</div></li><li><div>Potion of healing</div></li><li><div>Necklace of fireballs</div></li><li><div>Tome of Leadership &amp; Influence</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Dead halflings can have a ton of loot, as well as the dead hydra’s lair. There are dead war pigs everywhere. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">GREAT POWERS MOVING</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Amergin, the halfling paladin, will let the party know that her party was seeking out The Black City when they were attacked by Shadar-Kai, elves who have been taken over by the Raven Queen and are essentially undead. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Tinuviel, the Hamadryad</span> de facto ruler of Cendriane, appears in the swamp, alongside <span style="font-weight: bold;">Cassandra, the elven high priestess</span> of the Spirits.</div><dd style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"></dd><div><br/></div><div>When all of them are gathered, the party learns that the great powers of the world have awakened to the reality of the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Vulparia</span>, <span style="font-weight: bold;">Rhaeda’s</span> patron, hid the existence of the Raven Queen from the Fey Court. There is now maneuvering to take away Vulparia’s power and influence. Various fey factions will vie for Rhaeda’s service. They have learned that a great deal of Vulparia’s treasure has been delivered by Rhaeda’s family, and other fey will offer better terms if Rhaeda is open to it. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><font color="#ff2600">BREAKING THE BOND</font></b></div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen’s bond can be broken by swearing allegiance to a power capable of breaking that bond. As long as a being swears allegiance to the Raven Queen, she has power over life and death. </div><div><br/></div><div>When a being swears fealty to another great power (The Creator, a Spirit, or an Archfey), that being can break the Raven Queen’s power, but that may not be true forever. </div><div><br/></div><div>The problem is getting that being to exercise power on their behalf. They must show fealty in some way by serving that being in some significant way. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel knows the Shadar-Kai and the Raven Queen have created cells to infiltrate each major kingdom. They are planning to assassinate, destabilize, and turn every kingdom. She warns the party about the Black City, that the assassins they will face will be not only powerful but numerous. An entire city full of creatures that walk in the shadow, who respawn when they die. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - kill the magic item transporters and steal their magic items, assassinate King Darian XV</div></li><li><div>Ghealdar - kill the mid-rank officers in Ghealdar, where they’re more vulnerable. </div></li><ul><li><div>This has angered the Tuatha De. They want to go after Gibard directly. </div></li></ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - kill or reward the young dragons. So far they’ve gotten to Zel. There may be others. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">SAVE CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Amergen will recognize that Crow has begun the descent into becoming as the Shadar-Kai are. She will say that Crow must seek a way of being saved. </div><div><br/></div><div>One alternate way to do this is to find the wizard who created Cro, who happens to be related to Isadorae. He’s a gnome tinker who was last seen in the Engineering School, but disappeared years ago. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; color: rgb(4, 51, 255);">CONTINUING ON TO THE BLACK CITY</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Increasingly difficult combats with Shadar Kai. More sophisticated ambushes and warnings. If the party makes it into the Black City, they will need to avoid all Shadar Kai, as they will coordinate to bring the party down and force them into service to the Raven Queen or kill them. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><font color="#0433ff">THE SWAMP NEAR TAL’EOWAN’S MANOR</font></b></div><div><br/></div><div>If the party goes back here, Tinuviel will transport them directly into the swamp. The party will be facing Zel, a Young Black Dragon, with virtually unlimited goblin minions. This will be a mostly RP encounter, as defeating Zel will be a real challenge and even if they do, they must convince Zel to give up his allegiance to the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; color: rgb(4, 51, 255);">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>ZEL, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>Tine, a Fire dragon named after the spirit of fire, lives deep in the Kjeldoran mountains</div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Redwood trees encounter</title>
    <created>20191219T234719Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212328Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <source>mobile.iphone</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Large rings of redwoods surround long dead and disappeared trees. Those rings enable portals and summoning circles. </div><div><br/></div><div>In a massive storm, huge chunks of trees fall off, striking PCs and NPCs. Lightning strikes as well. </div><div><br/></div><div>There are redwoods that have been burning for months. The party needs to put out the fires in order to stop summoning. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Industrial Revolution in Atania</title>
    <created>20191226T231051Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212326Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>A small group of Atanian farmers have already started experimenting with farm equipment replicated by a goblin wizard from the School of Engineering. His name is <b>Ferrisduin</b>, a quiet, brilliant goblin scientist who sees magic as a way to make lives better. </div><div><br/></div><div>His artifact, The Tool Replicator, held under heavy guard at the Engineering School, is capable of replicating simple magical tools like hoes that never go dull or plows that pull themselves with simple guidance from a farmer. </div><div><br/></div><div>One of Ferrisduin’s assistants, a goblin scion of a wealthy Engineering family named <b>Semiote Hillhouse</b>, has begun using an early prototype of The Tool Replicator to recreate magic items at scale. Working at night, he cloned many magical wands. He hired an elven business associate by the name of <b>Scant McCarthy</b> who sells the weapons. Originally, Scant only sold to the goblins of Ghealdar, but with those goblins gaining their freedom, he began looking for new markets among the Free States and Atanian Organized Crime, specifically people who say they work for the Llyogoden, but who are also connected to the Thieves Guild, the Plain Stryd. </div><div><br/></div><div>Now that the wands have blown up, Semiote, Scant, and the Plain Stryd are going to be finding ways to cover themselves, and Ferrisduin will be dismayed and upset about the development. Semiote will try to get them back. Scant will cut all ties with the Plain Stryd. The Plain Stryd will kill anyone who gets too close. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 10</title>
    <created>20191209T164814Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212323Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>There are a number of wands available for the party to pocket/steal from the wagon. Each wand can cast Fireball 1d6+1 times before exploding. </div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center; ">####</div><div style="text-align: center; "><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Sadavir was seen in the crowd. Other dwarves in Atania recognize Sadavir Blessedarmor, but call him Sadavir Kinkiller. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Briar is part of the Sect of Tiathon. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Leader of the Gibbard - High Lord Commander Kayleigh. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Pox - Pony Ox. Orcish horses. They’re omnivorous. </div><div style="text-align: center; "><br/></div><div style="text-align: center; ">####</div><div><br/></div><div>With the eruption of a massive explosion and fire, the Atanian Garda show up almost instantly as the party is recovering. They will detain the party and bring in goblin engineer wizards to investigate the scene CSI-style. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Each party member will be separated and questioned behind a sound proof bubble. We will role-play that in front of everyone. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Leskyn (human), the NPC GARDA INVESTIGATOR </span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">NPC BARD / INTELLIGENCE OPERATIVE </span><span style="font-weight: bold;">Nurvar Durmak (half-Eladrin)</span></div><div><br/></div><div>He knows that the Engineering school has mass-manufacturing technology and needs help figuring out where the pipeline leads. Who is buying and who at the school is selling? </div><div><br/></div><div>The explosions become city-wide news, with every major faction in Atania having some interest in what happened. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Church will offer condolences, and send priests to learn more about the Raven Queen connection. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Garsun Valdun - CHURCH INQUISITOR NPC AND HOLY CHAMPION </span></div><div><br/></div><div>The Llygoden will try to entice the players to join up with them to protect the workers and non-fey. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">PROTEST ORGANIZER Coldshore</span><span style="font-weight: bold;"> (half-elf, excited true believer)</span> will present himself as a protest organizer, then gradually reveal he is a member of a secret organization called the <span style="font-weight: bold;">Llygoden</span>, tasked with keeping Atania safe &amp; accountable. He is actually a senior leader of the Plain Stryd, the thieves guild and children’s charity organization. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Bard College will want to know who the Raven Queen is so they can warn the people. They will send a powerful agent to offer help to spread the word of what’s happening. They can help verify the party’s account, and also offer magic transport to their next destination. </div><div><br/></div><div>The word of the Bard College will also go a long way toward convincing the other kingdoms to actually do something. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel knows the Shadar-Kai and the Raven Queen have created cells to infiltrate each major kingdom. They are planning to assassinate, destabilize, and turn every kingdom. She warns the party about the Black City, that the assassins they will face will be not only powerful but numerous. An entire city full of creatures that walk in the shadow, who respawn when they die. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - kill the magic item transporters and steal their magic items, assassinate King Darian XV</div></li><li><div>Ghealdar - kill the mid-rank officers in Ghealdar, where they’re more vulnerable. </div></li><ul><li><div>This has angered the Tuatha De. They want to go after Gibard directly. </div></li></ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - kill or reward the young dragons. So far they’ve gotten to Zel. There may be others. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVE CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Amergen will recognize that Crow has begun the descent into becoming as the Shadar-Kai are. She will say that Crow must seek a way of being saved. </div><div><br/></div><div>One alternate way to do this is to find the wizard who created Cro, who happens to be related to Isadorae. He’s a gnome tinker who was last seen in the Engineering School, but disappeared years ago. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SWAMP NEAR TAL’EOWAN’S MANOR</span></div><div><br/></div><div>If the party goes back here, Tinuviel will transport them directly into the swamp. The party will be facing Zel Rey Dios, a Young Black Dragon, with virtually unlimited goblin minions. This will be a mostly RP encounter, as defeating Zel will be a real challenge and even if they do, they must convince Zel to give up his allegiance to the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>Airgead, a silver dragon </div></li><li><div>Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 11</title>
    <created>20200102T215653Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212321Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Qualls Feather Token - Swan</div></li><li><div>Potion of Gaseous Form</div></li><li><div>Spell Scroll - Holy Weapon</div></li><li><div>Potion of Vitality</div></li><li><div>5 mini sculptures of orcish heroes. 250 gp each. </div></li><li><div>BONUS: +1 longsword</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Sadavir was seen in the crowd. Other dwarves in Atania recognize Sadavir Blessedarmor, but call him Sadavir Kinkiller. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Briar is part of the Sect of Tiathon. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Leader of Gibbard - High Lord Commander Kayleigh. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Pox - Pony Ox. Orcish horses. They’re omnivorous. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">27/150</div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">GIBARD, THE ORCISH FATHERS &amp; BREAG</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Silvermane and Draevan’s father, Drubag, has returned to Gibard, heralded as a heroic general who rallied the troops against a black dragon and drove it off. Their siblings, led by an orc named <span style="font-weight: bold;">Ugrash</span> found out Silvermane was in Gibard and sent a contingent of orcs to seek out Silvermane and see if he really set the dragon and the goblins loose. When they find out that Draevan is also Drubag’s get, they will welcome him into the family. </div><div><br/></div><div>When they find out Draevan killed a half-dozen orcs to save his mother, they will respect him even more. </div><div><br/></div><div>Unfortunately, the orcish guards who found Draevan and killed his mother are members of High Lord Commander Kayleigh’s personal bodyguard. They were friends with the orcs Draevan killed, and want payback. They have also sent orcs to kill Draevan. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(255, 38, 0); font-weight: bold;">5400 xp (Hard fight)</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">(2) Hobgoblin Devastator, Volo’s Guide p161. </span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">(1) Orc Blade of Ilneval (NAME </span><span style="color: rgb(255, 38, 0); font-weight: bold;">Kreneka</span><span style="font-weight: bold;">), (5) Claw of Luthic Volo’s 183</span></div><div><br/></div><div>The Tuatha De see the Brightshadows as traitors to the elven race. They’ve vowed to hunt them down and kill them off. When Breag goes to the Raven Queen, she will send Tuatha De with Breag to hunt down the party. She can carry two Tuatha De to fly after the party, or lead the assassins to the party. </div><div><br/></div><div>When/if the party is attacked and overwhelmed, Elaevan Brightshadow, an elven Revenant, will appear to assist the party, and have news that Drubag is in danger. Cassandra is behind Elaevan’s embrace of her revenant state. The party can also learn that Elaevan and Cassandra are in danger because the Raven Queen knows how to manipulate the energy of the dead, and they may lose their own free will. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel knows the Shadar-Kai and the Raven Queen have created cells to infiltrate each major kingdom. They are planning to assassinate, destabilize, and turn every kingdom. She warns the party about the Black City, that the assassins they will face will be not only powerful but numerous. An entire city full of creatures that walk in the shadow, who respawn when they die. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - kill the magic item transporters and steal their magic items, assassinate King Darian XV</div></li><li><div>Ghealdar - kill the mid-rank officers in Ghealdar, where they’re more vulnerable. </div></li><ul><li><div>This has angered the Tuatha De. They want to go after Gibard directly. </div></li></ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - kill or reward the young dragons. So far they’ve gotten to Zel. There may be others. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVE CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Amergen will recognize that Crow has begun the descent into becoming as the Shadar-Kai are. She will say that Crow must seek a way of being saved. </div><div><br/></div><div>One alternate way to do this is to find the wizard who created Cro, who happens to be related to Isadorae. He’s a gnome tinker who was last seen in the Engineering School, but disappeared years ago. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>Airgead, a silver dragon </div></li><li><div>Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 12 - 1/18/2020</title>
    <created>20200117T230541Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212318Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm’s lair</div><ul><li><div>11 small gems, 50 gp each</div></li><li><div>1100 gp</div></li><li><div>Boots of Speed</div></li><li><div>Cloak of Displacement</div></li><li><div>Clockwork amulet</div></li><li><div>+1 dagger</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Stone Giants</div><ul><li><div>Heward’s Handy Haversack</div></li><li><div>(inside the sack) 500 gp + 9 50 gp gems</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="caret-color: rgb(4, 51, 255);"><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">KJELDOR &amp; GORM</span></span></div><div><br/></div><div>A Kjeldoran elf named Finnleik Warysson, a bard in training, volunteers to lead the party on an expedition to Gorm’s lair. I claims to have come close to it and seen the dragon entering a cave filled with gold, gems and odd treasures. He is secretly a disciple of the Raven Queen, and leads the party into a group of Stone giants who don’t like people intruding into their territory. </div><div><br/></div><div>One of the stone giants, Saemond, actually knows where the lair is as well, if the party can get it out of him. </div><div><br/></div><div>Approaching the blue dragon’s lair will require working through snow, thunder and lightning. See the Regional Effects around Blue Dragons, and combine that with the giant encounters. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Stone Giant (3) </span>- MM 156. Finnleik leads the party to an ambush spot that gives the giants high ground advantage. Within the dragon’s territory, the party should be wary of air pockets in the snow as sinkholes. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">GORM - Young Blue Dragon</span> - Gorm will know the party is approaching because of the falcons, swifts, and jays that chirp warnings to it. Kobolds also wander the mountains, but scatter when the party sees them. </div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm goes and fetches allies. A stone giant. A shader kai. 20 kobolds. He knows the party is coming. </div><div><br/></div><div>Gloomweaver &amp; shadow dancer before the lair. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm thinks that he can resist the Raven Queen’s will when she calls in her favors for restoring him from death. He died fighting Airgead, a silver dragon who lives further North, when he tried to encroach on the older Silver dragon’s territory. He is very sensitive about losing the fight to Airgead and becomes defensive if it comes up. </div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm recently killed a set of Kjeldoran adventurers who wandered too close to his lair. They were friends with Finnleik, and when Finnleik went looking for them, he found an opportunity to ingratiate himself with a powerful, ambitious dragon, and bring the dragon new loot. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel knows the Shadar-Kai and the Raven Queen have created cells to infiltrate each major kingdom. They are planning to assassinate, destabilize, and turn every kingdom. She warns the party about the Black City, that the assassins they will face will be not only powerful but numerous. An entire city full of creatures that walk in the shadow, who respawn when they die. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - kill the magic item transporters and steal their magic items, assassinate King Darian XV</div></li><li><div>Ghealdar - kill the mid-rank officers in Ghealdar, where they’re more vulnerable. </div></li><ul><li><div>This has angered the Tuatha De. They want to go after Gibard directly. </div></li></ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - kill or reward the young dragons. So far they’ve gotten to Zel. There may be others. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVE CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Amergen will recognize that Crow has begun the descent into becoming as the Shadar-Kai are. She will say that Crow must seek a way of being saved. </div><div><br/></div><div>One alternate way to do this is to find the wizard who created Cro, who happens to be related to Isadorae. He’s a gnome tinker who was last seen in the Engineering School, but disappeared years ago. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>Airgead, a silver dragon </div></li><li><div>Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 13</title>
    <created>20200120T175243Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212316Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm’s lair</div><ul><li><div>11 small gems, 50 gp each</div></li><li><div>1100 gp</div></li><li><div>Boots of Speed</div></li><li><div>Cloak of Displacement</div></li><li><div>Clockwork amulet</div></li><li><div>+1 dagger</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Stone Giants</div><ul><li><div>Heward’s Handy Haversack</div></li><li><div>(inside the sack) 500 gp + 9 50 gp gems</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div><br/></div><div><font color="#0433ff"><span style="caret-color: rgb(4, 51, 255);"><b>FINNLEIK, GORM’S LAIR, THE RAVEN QUEEN BEGINS TO NOTICE THE PARTY</b></span></font></div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm is downed by the party, but not dead yet. The party can interrogate the dying dragon to find out about how he began worshipping the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm thinks that he can resist the Raven Queen’s will when she calls in her favors for restoring him from death. He died fighting Airgead, a silver dragon who lives further North, when he tried to encroach on the older Silver dragon’s territory. He is very sensitive about losing the fight to Airgead and becomes defensive if it comes up. </div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm recently killed a set of Kjeldoran adventurers who wandered too close to his lair. They were friends with Finnleik, and when Finnleik went looking for them, he found an opportunity to ingratiate himself with a powerful, ambitious dragon, and bring the dragon new loot. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel knows the Shadar-Kai and the Raven Queen have created cells to infiltrate each major kingdom. They are planning to assassinate, destabilize, and turn every kingdom. She warns the party about the Black City, that the assassins they will face will be not only powerful but numerous. An entire city full of creatures that walk in the shadow, who respawn when they die. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - kill the magic item transporters and steal their magic items, assassinate King Darian XV</div></li><li><div>Ghealdar - kill the mid-rank officers in Ghealdar, where they’re more vulnerable. </div></li><ul><li><div>This has angered the Tuatha De. They want to go after Gibard directly. </div></li></ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - kill or reward the young dragons. So far they’ve gotten to Zel. There may be others. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVE CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Amergen will recognize that Crow has begun the descent into becoming as the Shadar-Kai are. She will say that Crow must seek a way of being saved. </div><div><br/></div><div>One alternate way to do this is to find the wizard who created Cro, who happens to be related to Isadorae. He’s a gnome tinker who was last seen in the Engineering School, but disappeared years ago. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. <br/></div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 14 - Feb 8, 2020</title>
    <created>20200204T040427Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212312Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Gorm’s lair</div><ul><li><div>11 small gems, 50 gp each</div></li><li><div>1100 gp</div></li><li><div>Boots of Speed</div></li><li><div>Cloak of Displacement</div></li><li><div>Clockwork amulet</div></li><li><div>+1 dagger</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Stone Giants</div><ul><li><div>Heward’s Handy Haversack</div></li><li><div>(inside the sack) 500 gp + 9 50 gp gems</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;">Rope of Entanglement</div><div style="text-align: left;">Armor of Resistance (chain shirt)</div><div style="text-align: left;">Dimensional Shackles</div><div style="text-align: left;">Wand of the War Mage +2</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">25,000 gp</div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="caret-color: rgb(4, 51, 255); color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE MASTODON + FINNLEIK</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(255, 38, 0); font-weight: bold;">CHALLENGE</span>: loot the dragon’s lair while keeping the mastodon at bay and before it closes the portals. The summoned Mastodon will continue rampaging, attacking the party based on whoever’s closest to it. </div><div><br/></div><div>Finnleik is hiding in the dark. He will claim to have become terrified and hidden from the battle, planning to sneak away when things calmed down. Finnleik knows the following about the magic items &amp; bodies in the lair: </div><ul><li><div>A set of Kjeldoran adventurers told him they were going into the mountains to explore &amp; meet the new dragon</div></li><li><div>They left without him and he was too afraid to follow them</div></li><li><div>DC 20 persuasion/intimidate check: But secretly, he was part of the original group. He met Gorm, and was converted to worshipping the Raven Queen</div></li><li><div>The party still needs him as a guide in order to get out of the giant valley &amp; snows. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE KOBOLDS </span></div><div><br/></div><div>The party begins to rest, when the dragon comes back, resurrected by the Raven Queen, forcing them out into kobold tunnels that go through the mountains. The tunnels can be found with an investigation DC 12 Perception check. </div><div><br/></div><div>The tunnel winds in a long arc down, with a pressure plate that leads down a chute for anyone over 50 pounds. A DC 15 DEX check will avoid the chute. The chute drops any victims 40 feet into pitch-coated, moving spikes, and triggers the ringing of a series of bells. The moving spikes do 4d6 dmg. </div><div><br/></div><div>All climbing attempts impose disadvantage. A failed save means falling back on the spikes, doing damage again. </div><div><br/></div><div>Kobolds will appear on the round following the bells, armed with alchemist fire flasks, which inflict 1d4 fire damage, and ignite the pitch. Anyone caught in the pitch will take 2d6 fire damage per round they’re in the square, with 1d6 additional damage each round after leaving. </div><div><br/></div><div>The chute has a hidden door to the side of the 10x10 spike trap that the kobolds use to retrieve whatever falls down the chute. </div><div><br/></div><div>When the chute opens and the bells ring, even if none of the party falls down it, the Kobolds enter Tower Defense mode for anything coming down the ramp. Kobold guards armed with crossbows scavenged from Dwarven ruins will engage in hit and run shots to bait the party into <b>another chute</b> that drops into the same trap. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>SECTION 2</b></div><div><br/></div><div>At the end of the ramp, 40 feet down, there is a room that is disguised to look like a sorting room. There’s discarded detritus from the dragon lair, enough gold to look interesting, and some shiny broken hilts and other junk. The kobolds will make a show of defending their “vault” then escape, dropping portcullis on both sides. A DC 14 Str check will lift the portcullis, but in the meantime, the kobolds will continue attacking with crossbows. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>SECTION 3</b></div><div><br/></div><div>The kobolds will make their final stand after a series of rooms, within an old dwarven hall that provides plenty of cover for them. Throughout the hall there’s a series of falling log traps, pits, and poisoned needles, and ankle traps. Poison references <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Poisons#content">LINK</a>. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>poison DC 12, knock unconscious, awaken on damage or being slapped awake</div></li><li><div>falling logs DC 13, dmg 2d6 dmg</div></li><li><div>pits DC 13, dmg 1d10</div></li><li><div>ankle trap DC 13, immobilized for one round</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Upon exiting the kobold lair, the party will find a route to the surface, in a blinding snowstorm. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">All of these things end in a conversation with Tinuviel</span>, and transportation to the next dragon they need to kill. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel knows the Shadar-Kai and the Raven Queen have created cells to infiltrate each major kingdom. They are planning to assassinate, destabilize, and turn every kingdom. She warns the party about the Black City, that the assassins they will face will be not only powerful but numerous. An entire city full of creatures that walk in the shadow, who respawn when they die. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - kill the magic item transporters and steal their magic items, assassinate King Darian XV</div></li><li><div>Ghealdar - kill the mid-rank officers in Ghealdar, where they’re more vulnerable. </div></li><ul><li><div>This has angered the Tuatha De. They want to go after Gibard directly. </div></li></ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - kill or reward the young dragons. So far they’ve gotten to Zel. There may be others. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVING CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>One alternate way to do this is to find the wizard who created Cro, who happens to be related to Isadorae. He’s a gnome tinker named Cruthaigh who was last seen in the Engineering School, but disappeared years ago. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Amulet of Cog Control</span> doesn’t work because Cro is no longer Cog. When Cruthaigh tries to use it, Cog gets a saving throw DC 15 to resist commands. If he can get the amulet back, it will help him resist the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>(DEAD) Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>(DEAD) Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Magic Item tracking</title>
    <created>20191206T231051Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212301Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Tal’Aer’s ring was given to Sulpha. </div><div><br/></div><div>According to <a href="https://blogofholding.com/?p=7287">Blog of Holding</a>, the math works out to: </div><ul><li><div>Levels 1 - 4: 9 minor, 2 major</div></li><li><div>5 - 10: 28 and 6</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Evan - +1 two handed sword</div><div>Nicholas - +1 spear of the Shadar Kai + d6 necrotic damage (plus the Raven Queen’s attention)</div><div>Chris - scroll of mass healing, bag of beans</div><div>Adam - +1 Elven Chain (can’t use), Qualls Feather Token</div><div>Steve - </div><div>Charlie - magic shield </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">WISHLISTS</span></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Evan</span>: <span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">A cloak of displacement. Boots of speed. Belt of Dwarvenkind. Anything to boost armor without wearing armor. Any type of two handed weapon. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><span style="font-size: small; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-weight: bold;">Adam</span>: </span><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">As for a wishlist, Draeven's weapons are sacred to him since they belonged to his mother so I wouldn't want to replace them but would be stoked to enchant/enhance them along the way.  Oathbow would be badass, but that is a pretty high power item. Utility items like Boots/Cloak of Elvenkind, Immovable Rod, an Endless Quiver of +1 arrows, or Glamoured Studded Leather for some AC and utility.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><span style="font-size: small; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-weight: bold;">Chris</span> - </span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: small;"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">+1 magic weapon would be nice. 
</span></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">Belt of Hill Giant Strength
</span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">Winged Boots
</span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">Deck of Many Things (specifically looking for The Star Card)
</span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;"><br/></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><span style="font-size: small; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-weight: bold;">Nicholas</span> - </span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: small;"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">I’d say my top choice would be gauntlets of ogre power. They give me the same bonus to hit and damage as a +1 weapon, but boosts my strength, and I like to lift things. There’s also the issue that my weapons are reskinned, and it would feel a little contrived to find a magical double headed flower. Maybe if you would like to give me the magic weapons you can fasten them as a charm or something that I attach to the half of my weapon that transforms it (?)
</span></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><br/></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;">Magic armor is always good. I am currently wearing something that gives me AC 15, and allows me to use my +2 Dex bonus. So it would have to be better than that to be worthwhile.
</span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><br/></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><b>Charlie</b> - </span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><br/></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><br/></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><br/></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal;"><b>Steve</b> - </span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial;"><br/></span></div><div style="font-size: small; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial;">Necklace of Prayer Beads</span></div><div style="text-align: start;"><span style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial;">Belt of Dwarvenkind</span></div><div style="text-align: start;"><span style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial;">Periapt of Wound Closure</span></div><div style="text-align: start;"><span style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial;">Pearl of Power</span></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 16</title>
    <created>20200310T195525Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212258Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Magic shield, wielded by the Horned Devil. </div></li><li><div>Pearl of Power</div></li><li><div>+1 studded leather armor</div></li><li><div>10 gems, 100 gp each</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">CHRYSANIA AND THE DEMONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Chrysania will come back and ask the party to put a stop to the demons in the forest, and offer her help to do it. HEROES FEAST SPELL. While they’re doing that, she will travel to get assistance from the Fey Court with what’s happening in the Domhaine an Duine. </div><div><br/></div><div>Encounters: </div><ul><li><div>2 Shadow Demons (Eladrin), Barlgura (forest gorilla turned demonic), Hezrou (mulch creature w/ claws &amp; bite)</div></li><ul><li><div>Hezrou’s poison does 1d12 damage + poisoned condition for 1 hour</div></li></ul><li><div>1 Hezrou (mulch creature), Nycoloth (demonic moose) (MM pg 314)</div></li><li><div>1 Horned Devil, 4 Shadow Demons</div></li><ul><li><div>This leaves a Scarab of Death on the ground. <a href="https://www.dandwiki.com/wiki/SRD:Scarab_of_Death">https://www.dandwiki.com/wiki/SRD:Scarab_of_Death</a> </div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>The burning trees: </div><ul><li><div>There are 5 trees that are burning, plus one larger one in the center. </div></li><li><div>Each tree is roughly 100 feet high. Touching the trees inflicts 1d6 burning damage. Going inside the tree is 5d6 damage. Putting out the fires </div></li><li><div>Spells that could be useful: create water, control fire, control water, gust, </div></li><li><div>Lightning strikes the ground every 3 rounds, with a 20% chance of hitting a party member for 5d6 damage. </div></li><li><div>Closing the portal requires either a circle of protection from evil, forbiddance, or destroying the trees. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Meanwhile, The Shadar Kai Plot continues...</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - The Shadar Kai have stolen a cart full of magic items traveling from Atania to Ghealdar. All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><ul><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul><li><div>Ghealdar - mid-rank orcish officers are dying. The city is now under martial law, with Zel’s army of shadows &amp; goblins preparing to invade. </div></li><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. There are adventurers who are targeting the young, who will now be protected by older dragons. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVING CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutheigh has the amulet. The party may want to get it back. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Amulet of Cog Control</span> doesn’t work because Cro is no longer Cog. When Cruthaigh tries to use it, Cog gets a saving throw DC 15 to resist commands. If he can get the amulet back, it will help him resist the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>(RAISED AS A SHADOW DRAGON) Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 17</title>
    <created>20200324T164216Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212256Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Magical polearm for Nicholas, wielded by the Soul Monger</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">RETURNING TO GHEALDAR</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Ghealdar is under martial law. The party will appear in the middle of the orcish encampment, with a writ from Crysania and The Lady, Winter Queen of the Feywild. </div><div><br/></div><div>Orcish commander - Tur-og. </div><div><br/></div><div>Torg is still leading the goblins. It’s spiraled out of control and he’s gone back to the swamp to try to put a stop to it. He’s fighting against Zel &amp; Juice (Now Avenger of Souls). RELIGIEUSE </div><div><br/></div><div>The party will be asked to push into the Southern party of the city and find out how the goblins are positioned, and then into the jungle to figure out how they are positioned. </div><div><br/></div><div>Encounters: </div><ul><li><div>25 goblins who have taken a handful of orcs prisoner. Get them out without killing the goblins? </div></li><ul><li><div>The goblins turn into shadows - what happens to the orcs they kill? </div></li></ul><li><div>3 shader kai Shadow Dancers - REMEMBER THE SHADAR KAI HAVE EXTRA MAGIC ITEMS NOW</div></li><li><div>1 Gloom Weaver + 2 Shadow Dancers + 5 goblin shadows</div></li><li><div>1 Soul Monger + 1 shadow dancer + 10 goblin shadows</div></li><li><div>1 Shadow dragon (Zel'tanthalas) + 2 shadow dancers + 20 goblin shadows</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - The Shadar Kai have stolen a cart full of magic items traveling from Atania to Ghealdar. All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><ul><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds, then 1 round slow)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul><li><div>Ghealdar - mid-rank orcish officers are dying. The city is now under martial law, with Zel’s army of shadows &amp; goblins preparing to invade. </div></li><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. There are adventurers who are targeting the young, who will now be protected by older dragons. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVING CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutheigh has the amulet. The party may want to get it back. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Amulet of Cog Control</span> doesn’t work because Cro is no longer Cog. When Cruthaigh tries to use it, Cog gets a saving throw DC 15 to resist commands. If he can get the amulet back, it will help him resist the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>(RAISED AS A SHADOW DRAGON) Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 18</title>
    <created>20200404T161552Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212253Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div><br/></div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The Shadar Kai are sacrificing the goblins to the Raven Queen and Zel is eating their bodies. The party can tell they were slaughtered. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">War bands out of the swamp, trained goblins fighters, attacking the orcs. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Charbidis took off with Zel, investigating if the party is telling the truth about the Raven Queen. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Is Sarge still alive? Would he be willing/able to lead the goblins to peace with the orcs?</div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">RETURNING TO GHEALDAR</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Ghealdar is under martial law. The party will appear in the middle of the orcish encampment, with a writ from Crysania and The Lady, Winter Queen of the Feywild. </div><div><br/></div><div>Orcish commander - Tur-og. </div><div><br/></div><div>Torg is still leading the goblins. It’s spiraled out of control and he’s gone back to the swamp to try to put a stop to it. He’s fighting against Zel &amp; Juice (Now Avenger of Souls). RELIGIEUSE </div><div><br/></div><div>The party will be asked to push into the Southern party of the city and find out how the goblins are positioned, and then into the jungle to figure out how they are positioned. </div><div><br/></div><div>Encounters: </div><ul><li><div>25 goblins who have taken a handful of orcs prisoner. Get them out without killing the goblins? </div></li><ul><li><div>The goblins turn into shadows - what happens to the orcs they kill? </div></li></ul><li><div>3 shader kai Shadow Dancers - REMEMBER THE SHADAR KAI HAVE EXTRA MAGIC ITEMS NOW</div></li><li><div>1 Gloom Weaver + 2 Shadow Dancers + 5 goblin shadows</div></li><li><div>1 Soul Monger + 1 shadow dancer + 10 goblin shadows</div></li><li><div>1 Shadow dragon (Zel'tanthalas) + 2 shadow dancers + 20 goblin shadows</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - The Shadar Kai have stolen a cart full of magic items traveling from Atania to Ghealdar. All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><ul><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds, then 1 round slow)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul><li><div>Ghealdar - mid-rank orcish officers are dying. The city is now under martial law, with Zel’s army of shadows &amp; goblins preparing to invade. </div></li><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. There are adventurers who are targeting the young, who will now be protected by older dragons. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVING CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutheigh has the amulet. The party may want to get it back. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Amulet of Cog Control</span> doesn’t work because Cro is no longer Cog. When Cruthaigh tries to use it, Cog gets a saving throw DC 15 to resist commands. If he can get the amulet back, it will help him resist the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>(RAISED AS A SHADOW DRAGON) Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 20 - The Battle for Ghealdar</title>
    <created>20200604T044911Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212250Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Drow are good advanced versions of shadow dancers. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The orcs need to rally to protect the runegate. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The Raven Queen vowed to repay Cog for his insolence. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE BATTLE FOR GHEALDAR</span></div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen has launched an attack on Ghealdar. She aims to decapitate the orcish army by killing its most important generals. </div><div><br/></div><div>Orcish generals to protect</div><ul><li><div>General Tur-Og, the general in charge of Ghealdar</div></li><li><div>General Muunokhoi</div></li><li><div>General Temujin </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>ENCOUNTERS - 16,800 XP HARD / 11,200 MEDIUM / 73,500 DAILY</div><ul><li><div>Orc Command Tent: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wave 1: Shadowdancer (2), Death Slaad, Gloom weaver </div></li><li><div>Wave 2: Drow Shadowblade, 1 assassin, Soul Monger</div></li></ul><li><div>Street Fight: Archmage, Dao, Shadows</div></li><li><div>Street Fight 2: Warlock of the Raven Queen, Red Shadow Dragon (Raven), Assassins (2), shadows</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - The Shadar Kai have stolen a cart full of magic items traveling from Atania to Ghealdar. All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><ul><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds, then 1 round slow)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul><li><div>Ghealdar - mid-rank orcish officers are dying. The city is now under martial law, with Zel’s army of shadows &amp; goblins preparing to invade. </div></li><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. There are adventurers who are targeting the young, who will now be protected by older dragons. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVING CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutheigh has the amulet. The party may want to get it back. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Amulet of Cog Control</span> doesn’t work because Cro is no longer Cog. When Cruthaigh tries to use it, Cog gets a saving throw DC 15 to resist commands. If he can get the amulet back, it will help him resist the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>(RAISED AS A SHADOW DRAGON) Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 19</title>
    <created>20200419T221101Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212248Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Amulet</div></li><li><div>2 cleric scrolls - mass healing word, mass cure wounds</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Is Sarge still alive? Would he be willing/able to lead the goblins to peace with the orcs?</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The sharks run the shipyards. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Kayleigh’s niece - Jessica</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Tonet - Asher’s cousin. Tonet &amp; Jessica are smuggling things into Ghealdar. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Torg is now angry at Silvermane for calling him evil. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Chunky Turtle pub</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">WHAT DO TORG &amp; SARGE DO - FIGHTING OFF MORE SHADAR KAI? </div><ul><li><div style="text-align: left;">Torg and Sarge are holding off more Shadar Kai</div></li><li><div style="text-align: left;">When Juice is near dead, he calls upon the Raven Queen to summon a shadow dragon</div></li><li><div style="text-align: left;">Torg will sacrifice himself to distract the shadow dragon while the party goes after Juice</div></li></ul><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">RECALCULATE THE XP FOR THIS BATTLE</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">What did Briar do after guiding Juice’s soul to the Creator? </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The city of Ghealdar is under attack from a phalanx of Raven Queen warriors. A visage of the queen herself flies over the city in a raven. </div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">19k xp</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Shadow Dragon</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Soul Monger </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Shadows</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">LEADING TORG BACK TO GHEALDAR</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Torg is still leading a portion of the goblins, who have now split into factions. 3/4 of them follow The Avenger of Souls. Torg doesn’t believe himself a leader, and wants Sarge to take over leadership. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">FINDING SARGE</span></div><div><br/></div><div>The massive goblin has gone to ground in the Dump. He has protected status as the brother of the leader, but he is effectively under house arrest. The party can find him quite easily, but convincing him to turn against his brother will require some extensive roleplaying. He doesn’t believe the goblins can win, but he would rather die than live the way they’ve been living. He believes the Creator has turned against goblin-kind. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>One idea: help the orcs stop the goblins/shadows/shadar-kai who are assassinating orcish officers. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>If the party cannot persuade Sarge, the orcs march into the Southern part of the city, crushing the goblins and seizing Rutherford’s estate, killing the Avenger of Souls and hundreds of goblins with him. </div><div><br/></div><div>When the happens, the Raven Queen will send a Red shadow dragon to rescue The Avenger of Souls, who will flee South to the swamp, and then East to a retreat on the Thir, where he will spend time summoning undead to attack Ghealdar. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - The Shadar Kai have stolen a cart full of magic items traveling from Atania to Ghealdar. All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><ul><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds, then 1 round slow)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul><li><div>Ghealdar - mid-rank orcish officers are dying. The city is now under martial law, with Zel’s army of shadows &amp; goblins preparing to invade. </div></li><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. There are adventurers who are targeting the young, who will now be protected by older dragons. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">SAVING CRO</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutheigh has the amulet. The party may want to get it back. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Amulet of Cog Control</span> doesn’t work because Cro is no longer Cog. When Cruthaigh tries to use it, Cog gets a saving throw DC 15 to resist commands. If he can get the amulet back, it will help him resist the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>(RAISED AS A SHADOW DRAGON) Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 21 - Battle for Ghealdar, continued</title>
    <created>20200419T221101Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212245Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Next up: go to the Black City. Get intelligence to inform the orcs on how big of an army to bring. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Get the orcs to warn/inform the Free States. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Help ensure Torg/Sarge end up on the City Council. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Will the orcs help rebuild Ghealdar? What will the city council do? </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Draevan wants to raise an orcish army to attack the Raven Queen while also supporting an elvish uprising to retake the Hartland forest. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Speak with the dead: Isadorae? &lt;&lt;Is she friendly or not? </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Draevan: Krenica’s Crest - the bodyguard of Keyleigh. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Are there elvish enclaves outside of the Hartland that will help the Tuatha De? Who are they and where are they? There’s an embassy in Atania. He can also talk to Cassandra. He will tell her about what’s happening, and suggest that when the orcs invade the Saeserin, the elves should reclaim their heritage. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE BATTLE FOR GHEALDAR</span></div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen has launched an attack on Ghealdar. She aims to decapitate the orcish army by killing its most important generals. </div><div><br/></div><div>Orcish generals to protect</div><ul><li><div>General Tur-Og, the general in charge of Ghealdar</div></li><li><div>General Muunokhoi - </div></li><li><div>General Temujin - killed by a shadow mastiff </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>ENCOUNTERS - 16,800 XP HARD / 11,200 MEDIUM / 73,500 DAILY</div><ul><li><div>Street Fight 2: Warlock of the Raven Queen (Isadorae), Red Shadow Dragon (Raven), Assassins (2), shadows</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Atania - The Shadar Kai have stolen a cart full of magic items traveling from Atania to Ghealdar. All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><ul><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds, then 1 round slow)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul><li><div>Ghealdar - </div></li><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Black Raven outposts - kill the trade leaders, sow discord among the merchants</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. There are adventurers who are targeting the young, who will now be protected by older dragons. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">PURSUING THE DRAGONS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel promises to bring the party weaponry that can be used against dragons. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>(RAISED AS A SHADOW DRAGON) Zel, Young Adult Black Dragon</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Gorm, a Young Adult Blue Dragon near the Kjeldoran mountains and Kingdom of Gibard</div></li><li><div>(RAISED w/ powers) Breag, Young Green Dragon that lives within the kingdom of Gibard. </div></li><li><div>Tine and Airgead, Red and Silver dragons who’ve been friends since they were very small, live deep in the Kjeldoran mountains. They came to the Raven Queen together, as best friends. </div></li></ul><div></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 22 - Interregnum</title>
    <created>20200419T221101Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212243Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE GAZE OF THE RAVEN QUEEN </span></div><div><br/></div><div>The Queen has seen the party, is aware of them, and now desires to destroy them. They’ve destroyed her powerful agents, including Isadorae, Juice, and several of the dragons. </div><div><br/></div><div>Draevan wants to raise an orcish army to attack the Raven Queen while also supporting an elvish uprising to retake the Hartland forest. He is able to push this with Krenica’s Crest. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Speak with the dead: Isadorae?</span> </div><ul><li><div>She is kindly disposed toward the party</div></li><li><div>She knows very little about the Queen</div></li><li><div>She has seen a great army in the Black City</div></li><li><div>There is a darkness in the center of the city that cannot be penetrated, souls are pulled into that darkness that never return</div></li><li><div>There are shadow creatures that are capable of imitating nearly anyone. </div></li><li><div>There are shadow creatures that The Raven Queen can pull into our realm that are more dangerous than any mortal can possibly imagine - and if the party keeps questioning after this, one of those creatures will be pulled into the area. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Who are the Raven Queens Generals?</div><ul><li><div>Death Tyrant, Derukoskai</div></li><li><div>Gorm, Blue Dragon</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Shadow Plane</span></div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen will pull the party into a portal that detours into the Shadow Realm. </div><div><br/></div><div>The party sees strange visions, shadows of death and destruction in the free states. Animated corpses walking around, tearing down and destroying fortifications built by the orcs, with a terrible shadow growing larger and looming over the entire thing. </div><div><br/></div><div>If the party decides to stop this looming shadow they wind up fighting a Death Tyrant in the ruins of the free state of Adare. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Dragons Avenge - G</span><span style="font-weight: bold;">orm, Breag and others</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Demand the orcs release the party to their care. In the melee, Charbidis shows up to rescue them. a schism grows between the dragons. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Ghealdar </div></li><ul><li><div>Goblins are free, and the City Council will now allow goblins to enter into contracts with other citizens. </div></li><li><div>Sarge will be given a spot on the city council. </div></li><li><div>The orcs will hire goblin engineers to help rebuild Ghealdar</div></li></ul><li><div>Atania - shadow versions of the party are being seen around Atania. </div></li><ul><li><div>All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds, then 1 round slow)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>Are there elvish enclaves outside of the Hartland that will help the Tuatha De? Who are they and where are they? There’s an embassy in Atania. He can also talk to Cassandra. He will tell her about what’s happening, and suggest that when the orcs invade the Saeserin, the elves should reclaim their heritage. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Free States are in a panic, preparing for war, and trying to close their borders (wholly unsuccessfully). </div></li><li><div>They’ve received info from the orcs. </div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><ul><li><div>The orcs are concerned that they can’t leave their entire border unsecured. They need to keep a portion of their troops back. </div></li></ul><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. Unfortunately for the heroes, shadow versions of themselves are being seen throughout the land, attacking dragons and haunting Atanian strongholds. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 23 - Derukoskai</title>
    <created>20200804T141046Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212240Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The party wants to go help Charbidis fight the dragons and have him nuke the town. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The small dragons are allied with the Derukoskai, and will come to his aid. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">Breag can tell the party which dragons are aligned with the Raven Queen. The party refused and he warned them that what Charbidis did to Duine, the other dragons will do to the mortal lands. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><font color="#ff2600">Party arrived in Adare, wants to speak to the mayor. They need to warn the town about the impending undead attack. </font></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE GAZE OF THE RAVEN QUEEN </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Who are the Raven Queens Generals?</div><ul><li><div>Death Tyrant, Derukoskai</div></li><li><div>Gorm, Adult Blue Dragon - aged up by The Raven Queen. </div></li><ul><li><div>Dust devils </div></li><li><div>Air elementals</div></li><li><div>“Shadow” giants = Storm Giants. The Storm Giant from Dragonshome peak is Amgeror. </div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>Near Adare, three Shadow Giants have created a horrible storm to cover the approach of the Raven Queen’s armies. The storm covers 5 miles approaching Adare in any direction so that nobody knows where the weather is coming from. </div><div><br/></div><div>Derukoskai is a Death Tyrant that is leading the Raven Queen’s armies as they slowly swallow the Free States. </div><div><br/></div><div>ENCOUNTERS in Duine: </div><ul><li><div>Death Tyrant, Vampire Spellcaster, Ogre Zombie, Bone naga, Revenant x2</div></li><li><div>Vampire Warrior, Vampire Spawn x2, Revenant x2, Mummy x3</div></li><li><div>Rakshasa, Death Slaad x2</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Dragons Avenge - G</span><span style="font-weight: bold;">orm, Breag and others</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Demand the orcs release the party to their care. In the melee, Charbidis shows up to rescue them. a schism grows between the dragons. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>The plot for each kingdom: </div><ul><li><div>Ghealdar </div></li><ul><li><div>Goblins are free, and the City Council will now allow goblins to enter into contracts with other citizens. </div></li><li><div>Sarge will be given a spot on the city council. </div></li><li><div>The orcs will hire goblin engineers to help rebuild Ghealdar</div></li></ul><li><div>Atania - shadow versions of the party are being seen around Atania. </div></li><ul><li><div>All Shadar Kai the party encounters will now be equipped with poorly functioning, extra magic items. </div></li><li><div>Mass-manufactured magic items include: </div></li><ul><li><div>Wand of Fireball</div></li><li><div>Scrolls of </div></li><li><div>Potions of haste (2 rounds, then 1 round slow)</div></li><li><div>Potions of Cloud Giant Strength (2 rounds, then disadvantage on all Str/Dex for 2 rounds)</div></li></ul></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>Are there elvish enclaves outside of the Hartland that will help the Tuatha De? Who are they and where are they? There’s an embassy in Atania. He can also talk to Cassandra. He will tell her about what’s happening, and suggest that when the orcs invade the Saeserin, the elves should reclaim their heritage. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Free States are in a panic, preparing for war, and trying to close their borders (wholly unsuccessfully). </div></li><li><div>They’ve received info from the orcs. </div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><ul><li><div>The orcs are concerned that they can’t leave their entire border unsecured. They need to keep a portion of their troops back. </div></li></ul><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. Unfortunately for the heroes, shadow versions of themselves are being seen throughout the land, attacking dragons and haunting Atanian strongholds. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 24</title>
    <created>20200901T043648Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212237Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">DON’T FORGET THE TREASURE REWARDS</span></div><div><br/></div><div>In Adare, the party has access to a treasure trove</div><ul><li><div>Wand of the War Mage</div></li><li><div>Javelin of Lightning +1</div></li><li><div>Ioun Stone (mastery) yellow<br/></div></li><li><div>Stone of Good Luck purple </div></li><li><div>Ring of Evasion (2 charges) </div></li><li><div>Wand of Paralysis</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####NOTES</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: center;">####</div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE FREE STATES</span></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">In the middle of the blizzard, Adare is hunkering down, but panicked. The mayor, John Uldine, has no idea what to do. The Free States don’t have any magical resources to fight off what’s coming. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><ul><li><div style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">Amgeror the Storm Giant + 2 winter wolves</span></div></li></ul><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Battle of Adare</span></div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><div style="text-align: left;">The elvish spirits who serve the Raven Queen and died in her service have risen to wreak vengeance upon the party. One of them, a Death Knight, is leading a troop of undead elves to destroy Draevan &amp; the party. </div><div style="text-align: left;"><br/></div><ul><li><div style="text-align: left;">Revenant x6, Banshee x2</div></li><li><div style="text-align: left;">Death Knight, Revenant x4, Wraith x 2</div></li><li><div style="text-align: left;">Ice Devil, Frost Giant x3</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE GAZE OF THE RAVEN QUEEN </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Who are the Raven Queens Generals?</div><ul><li><div>Death Tyrant, Derukoskai</div></li><li><div>Gorm, Adult Blue Dragon - aged up by The Raven Queen. </div></li><ul><li><div>Dust devils </div></li><li><div>Air elementals</div></li><li><div>“Shadow” giants = Storm Giants. The Storm Giant from Dragonshome peak is <span style="font-weight: bold; color: rgb(4, 51, 255);">Amgeror</span>. </div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><span style="color: rgb(4, 51, 255); font-weight: bold;">THE SHADAR-KAI PLOT </span></div><div><br/></div><div>Tinuviel has disappeared into the darkness, seemingly consumed by the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div>Are there elvish enclaves outside of the Hartland that will help the Tuatha De? Who are they and where are they? There’s an embassy in Atania. Draevan can also talk to Cassandra. He will tell her about what’s happening, and suggest that when the orcs invade the Saeserin, the elves should reclaim their heritage. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Free States</div></li><ul><li><div>The Free States are in a panic, preparing for war, and trying to close their borders (wholly unsuccessfully). </div></li><li><div>The goblins are stuck in the blizzard</div></li></ul><li><div>Gibard - targeted assassinations, torching encampments around the edges, where some elves still live and claim holy sites. </div></li><ul><li><div>The orcs are concerned that they can’t leave their entire border unsecured. They need to keep a portion of their troops back. </div></li></ul><li><div>The Dragon Council - has issued an edict that adventurers are no longer allowed to attack young dragons. Unfortunately for the heroes, shadow versions of themselves are being seen throughout the land, attacking dragons and haunting Atanian strongholds. </div></li></ul><div><br/></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 25</title>
    <created>20200902T004927Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212235Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>How can the celestials exploit Cog’s connection to the Raven Queen? </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>Adam: </div><div><br/></div><div>I would present Krenika's crest as my street cred - showing that I have slain a high-placed orc. I would update them on the situation - the orcs' agreement to march on the Black City, the dragons' part in everything, the new issues with an entire town being turned, and the danger of the elves turning to Tuatha de. I think I would be interested to learn what the Elven leadership knows of the dark pacts made by desperate elves to the Raven Queen and how we could strategize keeping more from going to the dark side.</div><div><br/></div><div>I would suggest that the Elves be ready to act in the coming days. I had thought, initially, that I would be suggesting armed action against the orcs but, given the myriad of threats, I think it is too risky to act hastily. Being such a long-lived race I think the elves would fall in line with that idea. But, the elves should know how things are developing and that the day to act and make change is coming.</div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen enters the battlefield. She is terrible and horrifying. <a href="evernote:///view/1617575/s15/7f39a0d7-f36c-4a6f-bad6-a48eff8af1d1/7f39a0d7-f36c-4a6f-bad6-a48eff8af1d1/" style="color: rgb(105, 170, 53);">The Raven Queen stats</a> </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Ceann Ar Dtus Aingeal</span> - The First Angel Ceann - will appear on the battlefield and offer the party a way out if Briar prays. </div><div><br/></div><div>Ceann will bring the party to a realm full of light, a place close to the Creator. The party will be fully healed just by virtue of being there, but their weapons full of negative energy will being to dissolve. Ceann will tell them the following: </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>The being known as the Raven Queen was named <span style="font-weight: bold;">Banrion Fitheach</span>. She was with the Creator at the creation of the world, seeing the creation of the Domhain an Sidhe and Domhaine an Duine. The Sidhe were originally created as a separate race, the Djinn, who would be closer to the Creator, serving as intermediaries to the mortal races. </div></li><li><div>Banrion Fitheach corrupted the nature of the Djinn. She demanded dominion over them, and when she received it, it wasn’t enough. There was a schism between the Sidhe, creating the Unseelie and Seelie Sidhe. </div></li><li><div>As a way of protecting Domhain an Duine, the first Darian Bloodstone was given a sword, staff, and crown that allowed him to protect his realm from the Djinn. Cyric the Warlord stole the staff and used it to subject some of the Djinn to his will. At the end of the war, on Dragonshome peak, Darian shattered the staff with the sword, destroying both of them. </div></li><li><div>When Darian left Domhaine an Duine he brought the broken items. They were stored here in this realm of alabaster stone and celestial beings. The current King Darian X was gifted the Crown. The Djinn are being used by him to enrich the kingdom. </div></li><ul><li><div>Is there a Djinn that stole the crown and wants to bring it to the Raven Queen? </div></li></ul><li><div>The heavens have called Briar to this moment. Her faith and humility have made her a holy warrior for the Creator to right the wrong that The Raven Queen created - people not going to their eternal rest. </div></li><li><div>The party was brought to Neamh, the Celestial realm, to gift them with the reforged sword and the repaired staff, and to retrieve the crown to defeat the Raven Queen. </div></li><li><div>The staff is missing from its resting place in Neamh, and the sword is still broken. The Djinn who was supposed to reforge the sword is missing, with the pieces on the floor of the forge. The staff pieces are missing. The party can describe The Raven Queen’s staff and Ceann will recognize it as the Staff of Djinn. </div></li><ul><li><div>The angel is not dead yet, but dying. He flings the pommel of the sword into another celestial realm. As he dies he tells the party where he flung it. </div></li><li><div>Make Brian’s character learn how to reforge the sword. </div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>When the party discovers the missing artifacts, it will be inside of a forge powered by <span style="font-weight: bold;">Efreeti</span>. The forge Angel is broken, allied to the Raven Queen after listening to the Efreeti for hundreds of years, attempting to discover how to escape. They will attack the party in vengeance for their imprisonment. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>Allow no more than a short rest before the fight. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Barachiel Donnu</span>, the Angel of the Forge, is the name of the Empyrean angel that was supposed to forge the Sword of Darian. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>Artifacts</div><div><br/></div><div>Crown of Darian</div><div><br/></div><div>Sword of Darian</div><div><br/></div><div>Staff of the Djinn </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 27</title>
    <created>20201028T010928Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212233Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Sadavir made a vow the Dwarves Forge Gods that he would destroy The Raven Queen</div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>Allow no more than a short rest before the fight. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Barachiel Donnu</span>, the Angel of the Forge. </div><div><br/></div><div>Barachiel tells them that the sword can only be reforged by gathering rare ingredients: the claw of a golden dragon. It was forged by pulling a claw from <span style="font-weight: bold;">Ag Taitnham Laghairt, or The Shining Dragon</span>, Darian Bloodstone’s dragon companion.  It can only be quenched in the blood of a djinn. Barachiel will not do that. </div><div><br/></div><div>These are all lies of course. He will send the party on a lark to buy the Raven Queen more time. The sword can be reforged here in this room, but it must be heated to the same heat as the lava, which will destroy the party, but Barachiel will not tell them how to quench the sword (a cone of cold or equivalent spell will do it). </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>In order to figure out how to change Cog, they will have to find Crutha and bring him to the forge. While looking for his lair, the party will be attacked by another dragon. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">Artifacts</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Crown of Darian - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div>Sword of Darian - +3 Holy Avenger sword. Dominate Monster (Djinn) 1/long rest. Can be used in a ritual version of the spell, causing the duration to extend to one week for up to 3 Djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div>Staff of the Djinn - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 26</title>
    <created>20200902T004927Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212230Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Why did the Celestial send the party to get a dragon claw? </div><ul><li><div>Cog</div></li><ul><li><div>Build a monument?</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>The party found out that the staff was a deception, the sword was not destoyed in the forge but thrown into the ocean in the Feywild, and the King has the Crown. </div><div><br/></div><div>The party thinks Cassandra has possibly betrayed the party. </div><div><br/></div><div>Who knew the staff was buried with Cyric? </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>How can the celestials exploit Cog’s connection to the Raven Queen? </div><div><br/></div><div>The lava in the room is a hazard in addition to the firestorm. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen enters the battlefield. She is terrible and horrifying. <a href="evernote:///view/1617575/s15/7f39a0d7-f36c-4a6f-bad6-a48eff8af1d1/7f39a0d7-f36c-4a6f-bad6-a48eff8af1d1/" style="color: rgb(105, 170, 53);">The Raven Queen stats</a> </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">The Ceann Ar Dtus Aingeal</span> - The First Angel Ceann - will appear on the battlefield and offer the party a way out if Briar prays. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>The staff is missing from its resting place in Neamh, and the sword is still broken. The Djinn who was supposed to reforge the sword is missing, with the pieces on the floor of the forge. The staff pieces are missing. The party can describe The Raven Queen’s staff and Ceann will recognize it as the Staff of Djinn. </div></li><ul><li><div>The angel is not dead yet, but dying. He flings the pommel of the sword into another celestial realm. As he dies he tells the party where he flung it. </div></li><li><div>Make Brian’s character learn how to reforge the sword. </div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>When the party discovers the missing artifacts, it will be inside of a forge powered by <span style="font-weight: bold;">Efreeti</span>. The forge Angel is broken, allied to the Raven Queen after listening to the Efreeti for hundreds of years, attempting to discover how to escape. They will attack the party in vengeance for their imprisonment. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>Allow no more than a short rest before the fight. </div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold;">Barachiel Donnu</span>, the Angel of the Forge, is the name of the Empyrean angel that was supposed to forge the Sword of Darian. He has decided that the Raven Queen is right to free the Djinn. The Forge stops working as the staff and sword leave. </div><div><br/></div><div>Barachiel will beg for his life when the party has him at less than 20% HP. He has lived since the dawn of time, and his death here means certain destruction forever. He will tell the party about how the Efreet told him their stories over and over for millennia, begging to be freed, but the Angels have refused to let them go. The Raven Queen is only freeing her people from unjust imprisonment. </div><div><br/></div><div>Barachiel tells them that the sword can only be reforged by gathering rare ingredients: the claw of a golden dragon. It was forged by pulling a claw from <span style="font-weight: bold;">Ag Taitnham Laghairt, or The Shining Dragon</span>, Darian Bloodstone’s dragon companion.  It can only be quenched in the blood of a djinn. Barachiel will not do that. </div><div><br/></div><div>These are all lies of course. He will send the party on a lark to buy the Raven Queen more time. The sword can be reforged here in this room, but it must be heated to the same heat as the lava, which will destroy the party, but Barachiel will not tell them how to quench the sword (a cone of cold or equivalent spell will do it). </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>They want to take a claw from Charbidis. </div><div><br/></div><div>Bring Crutha to the forge to help forge the weapon? </div><div><br/></div><div>What is on the top of Dragonshome peak? The Raven Queen, raiding Cyric’s tomb. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">Artifacts</span></div><div><br/></div><div>Crown of Darian - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div>Sword of Darian - +3 Holy Avenger sword. Dominate Monster (Djinn) 1/long rest. Can be used in a ritual version of the spell, causing the duration to extend to one week for up to 3 Djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div>Staff of the Djinn - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 28</title>
    <created>20201028T010928Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212227Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Sadavir made a vow the Dwarves Forge Gods that he would destroy The Raven Queen</div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Celestial Forge</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Barachiel Donnu</b>, the Angel of the Forge. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Angelic Choir has sent someone to investigate Barachiel and that being is seeking out the party to figure out which lies he told them. That agent could be Nicholas’ character. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">Crutha + the transformation of Cog</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutha will help the party figure out how to transform Cog. </div><ul><li><div>The Gem of Djinn Control</div></li><li><div>The Celestial Forge</div></li><li><div>A Level 7 Magic Jar spell, modified to work for others</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>At the Celestial Forge, when Crutha is about to cast Magic Jar, he will attempt to put himself into the Gem and the party will have to figure out how to stop him </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Feywild Ocean </span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>A Kraken?</b></div><div><br/></div><div>Several Marid, controlling a huge host of water elementals</div><ul><li><div>Make heavy use of Control Water in order to keep away the gem</div></li><li><div>Give the Marid’s Dispel Magic in order to dispel any water breathing effects the party has cast </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b><u>Artifacts</u></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>Sword of Darian</b> - +3 Holy Avenger sword. Dominate Monster (Djinn) 1/long rest. Can be used in a ritual version of the spell, causing the duration to extend to one week for up to 3 Djinn. <b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 29</title>
    <created>20201115T044132Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212225Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>Sadavir made a vow the Dwarves Forge Gods that he would destroy The Raven Queen</div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Celestial Forge</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Barachiel Donnu</b>, the Angel of the Forge. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Angelic Choir has sent someone to investigate Barachiel and that being is seeking out the party to figure out which lies he told them. That agent could be Nicholas’ character. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">Crutha + the transformation of Cog</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutha will help the party figure out how to transform Cog. </div><ul><li><div>The Gem of Djinn Control</div></li><li><div>The Celestial Forge</div></li><li><div>A Level 7 Magic Jar spell, modified to work for others</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>At the Celestial Forge, when Crutha is about to cast Magic Jar, he will attempt to put himself into the Gem and the party will have to figure out how to stop him. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crutha stats</b></div><div><br/></div><div>Round 1: Timestop, Gate, Animate, Globe of Invulnerability (5th level spells)</div><div>Round 2: Mass polymorph</div><div>Round 3: Feeblemind</div><div>Round 4: Forcecage</div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Summons: </div></li><ul><li><div>Is able to animate nearby objects to fight for him. </div></li><ul><li><div>Anvil, Hammer, and tongs</div></li><li><div>Celestial radiant weapons</div></li><li><div>Shields that protect him </div></li></ul></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Feywild Ocean </span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>A Kraken?</b></div><div><br/></div><div>Several Marid, controlling a huge host of water elementals</div><ul><li><div>Make heavy use of Control Water in order to keep away the gem</div></li><li><div>Give the Marid’s Dispel Magic in order to dispel any water breathing effects the party has cast </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>Sword of Darian</b> - +3 Holy Avenger sword. Dominate Monster (Djinn) 1/long rest. Can be used in a ritual version of the spell, causing the duration to extend to one week for up to 3 Djinn. <b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 30</title>
