    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><b><span style="color:rgb(0, 131, 229);">Treasure from the Kraken's lair? </span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>The party opened a power vacuum in the Feywild. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>Sadavir made a vow the Dwarves Forge Gods that he would destroy The Raven Queen</div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Celestial Forge</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Barachiel Donnu</b>, the Angel of the Forge. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Angelic Choir has sent someone to investigate Barachiel and that being is seeking out the party to figure out which lies he told them. That agent could be Nicholas’ character. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">Crutha + the transformation of Cog</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutha will help the party figure out how to transform Cog. </div><ul><li><div>The Gem of Djinn Control</div></li><li><div>The Celestial Forge</div></li><li><div>A Level 7 Magic Jar spell, modified to work for others</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>At the Celestial Forge, when Crutha is about to cast Magic Jar, he will attempt to put himself into the Gem and the party will have to figure out how to stop him. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crutha stats</b></div><div><br/></div><div>Round 1: Timestop, Gate, Animate, Globe of Invulnerability (5th level spells)</div><div>Round 2: Mass polymorph</div><div>Round 3: Feeblemind</div><div>Round 4: Forcecage</div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Summons: </div></li><ul><li><div>Is able to animate nearby objects to fight for him. </div></li><ul><li><div>Anvil, Hammer, and tongs</div></li><li><div>Celestial radiant weapons</div></li><li><div>Shields that protect him </div></li></ul></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Feywild Ocean </span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>A Kraken?</b></div><div><br/></div><div>Several Marid, controlling a huge host of water elementals</div><ul><li><div>Make heavy use of Control Water in order to keep away the gem</div></li><li><div>Give the Marid’s Dispel Magic in order to dispel any water breathing effects the party has cast </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>Sword of Darian</b> - +3 Holy Avenger sword. Dominate Monster (Djinn) 1/long rest. Can be used in a ritual version of the spell, causing the duration to extend to one week for up to 3 Djinn. <b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 31</title>
    <created>20201115T044132Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212220Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><b><span style="color:rgb(0, 131, 229);">Treasure from the Kraken's lair? </span></b></div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Adam - Oathbow</div></li><li><div>Nicholas - ring of resistance (cold)</div></li><li><div>Charlie - pale lavender ioun stone </div></li><li><div>Steve - staff of healing</div></li><li><div>Evan - ioun stone awareness (dark blue rhomboid)</div></li><li><div>Brian</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>The party opened a power vacuum in the Feywild. The Pirate captain now has open access into the Fey sea and the river that goes up into the mountains and the Runegate there. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>Sadavir made a vow the Dwarves Forge Gods that he would destroy The Raven Queen. The dwarves gods will bless him with the skills to reforge Cog. </div><div><br/></div><div>The <b>Gem of Djinn</b> is sentient, and will try to control Silvermane. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">The Celestial Forge</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Barachiel Donnu</b>, the Angel of the Forge. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Angelic Choir has sent someone to investigate Barachiel and that being is seeking out the party to figure out which lies he told them. That agent could be Nicholas’ character. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;">Crutha + the transformation of Cog</span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>Crutha will help the party figure out how to transform Cog. </div><ul><li><div>The Gem of Djinn Control</div></li><li><div>The Celestial Forge</div></li><li><div>A Level 7 Magic Jar spell, modified to work for others</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>At the Celestial Forge, when Crutha is about to cast Magic Jar, he will attempt to put himself into the Gem and the party will have to figure out how to stop him. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crutha stats</b></div><div><br/></div><div>Round 1: Timestop, Gate, Animate, Globe of Invulnerability (5th level spells)</div><div>Round 2: Mass polymorph</div><div>Round 3: Feeblemind</div><div>Round 4: Forcecage</div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Summons: </div></li><ul><li><div>Is able to animate nearby objects to fight for him. </div></li><ul><li><div>Anvil, Hammer, and tongs</div></li><li><div>Celestial radiant weapons</div></li><li><div>Shields that protect him </div></li></ul></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div><b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 32</title>
    <created>20201222T064037Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212214Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>The <b>Gem of Djinn</b> is sentient, and will try to control Silvermane. </div><div><br/></div><div>“A Cluster***k of Counterspells”</div><div><br/></div><div>Chonk Lord the WetBlanket, Lord of 7th Realm of Noodles. </div><div><br/></div><div>Silvermane wants to touch the crown to get more information from the gems while they’re molten hot. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="color:rgb(4, 51, 255);">Atania &amp; the Crown</span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>The party must now turn their attention to Atania, the Crown of Darian, and the Raven Queen’s army invading the city. </div><div><br/></div><div>The party will need to go back and forth between looking for the crown and defending Atania. </div><div><br/></div><div>THE RAVEN QUEEN’S ARMY</div><ul><li><div>Shock troops</div></li><ul><li><div>Archmage</div></li><li><div>Death Knight</div></li><li><div>Pit Fiend</div></li><li><div>Mob: </div></li></ul><li><div>Special forces going for the crown</div></li><ul><li><div>Dark Elves as Tuatha De</div></li><li><div>When the mages die, they summon yochlol </div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div>When the party goes looking for the crown, King Darian X will let them know the crown is being used by the Engineering school to fabricate magic items. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><ul><li><div>5 members of the Atanian nobility are using the gems to manufacture weapons</div></li><li><div>The King publicly orders everyone bring the gems to the Engineering school. </div></li><ul><li><div>The spymaster secretly relays additional orders: bring decoys to the school, bring the real gems to the King’s palace</div></li></ul><li><div>6 gems, each has a Djinn trapped inside of it. The Raven Queen was released from it? </div></li><li><div>The party needs to destroy the Djinn on their native planes (the Elemental Djinn)</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 33</title>
    <created>20201222T064037Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212212Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>"Rocks do a lot of lying"</div><div><br/></div><div>"Will the shackles fit on a gerbil?" </div><div><br/></div><div>Advanced magic jar spell: the crown needs to touch  the Raven Queen while Cog casts Magic Jar.  The casting time of the spell is one minute. </div><div><br/></div><div>Magic Jar trap scenario. </div><div><br/></div><div>FORMULA FOR CALCULATING THE WEIGHT OF A 6" THICK STONE CIRCLE</div><div><br/></div><div>Magic shackles that prevents teleportation. </div><div><br/></div><div>Where is the Raven Queen located? </div><div><br/></div><div>Mass Polymorph scrolls for the party. </div><div><br/></div><div>Teleport to the Black City > Mass polymorph into ravens &amp; fly in > spam her with disabling effects > throw the anti-teleport shackles  and grapple her > force her into the gem </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>Silvermane wants to touch the crown to get more information from the gems while they’re molten hot. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="color:rgb(4, 51, 255);">The Engineering Guild rebuilds the Crown</span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>As the goblin engineers finish melding the crown together, Silvermane touches it to try to communicate with the djinn inside of it. Each djinn in the crown has their own story of woe and pain, having been entrapped for millenia. </div><div><br/></div><div>"You see a vast ocean, blue so deep and dark it's almost black. Light grows brighter as you near the surface. The water surges with you as you near the surface. Just on the other side of the water you can see the shores of the mighty river overflowing its banks. Dirt obscures the water until you break the surface. You are surging forward, reveling in the power of the overflowing river that carries you along. You effortlessly move between straw huts along the bank. You see the water surge through the huts and destroy them. You vaguely recall that the Duine lived in those huts, the Grandchildren of the Creator, but the surge is so exciting, and the Duine had agreed not to live that close to the river.</div><div><br/></div><div>Suddenly one of the Celestials is standing in front of you. You, and the water, crash against an invisible barrier of scintillating multicolored light, containing the surge. One of the angels holds a gem in front of you and speaks words of power. You know the words to counter them, but you are stunned from running into the magical barrier. Before you can recover, the world seemingly grows large as you realize you are shrinking. That's how you came to be in this gem." </div><div><br/></div><div>You hear a voice, "FREE ME!"</div><div><br/></div><div>You see similar scenes. Wildfires raging out of control stopped by imprisoning the djinn. Hurricanes destroying islands suddenly becalmed. An earthquake swallows the edge of a village but is brought to a sudden halt by a phalanx of angels. With each vision, you hear a primal voice shout FREE ME!</div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>The fifth vision is different. The fifth vision is war. Inside the celestial realm, outside a mighty fortress much like the one where you reforged Cog, you are laying siege to the Celestials. You shout for the release of our brothers. In the maelstrom of mighty divine magic, a legion of angels attacks. They carry with them the gems, pulling your sibling djinn into the gems. The shouts of your siblings die as they are entrapped. A voice shouts FREE ME. </div><div><br/></div><div>The sixth and final vision is different still. </div><div><br/></div><div>You see King Darian X. He is pleading with you to destroy this gem. He's a good man, you've answered many of his prayers over time, and his crown is bringing him nightmares. The beings inhabiting the crown have learned to cry out to this righteous king for justice. He begs you to take the crown. In mercy, you tell him that while it must remain in this realm, the crown can be changed. Perhaps by separating the beings they won't be able to create such discord. You bring the crown to the Engineer's guild and work with a goblin to break the crown into pieces - but suddenly something goes terribly wrong. The goblin has cracked one of the gems, and a being of immense power is attempting to escape. You begin to call upon your heavenly powers, but the being's chaos and strength overwhelm your faith and you find yourself...trapped. FREE ME!</div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>The angel trapped inside the final gem, formerly occupied by the Raven Queen, is named Oga. He is a young angel of little power, sent to comfort King Darian and carry messages. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>If the party breaks the gem, releasing Oga, he will tell them that the Raven Queen put him in there. He will tell them about the Shadowfell and that they can find her there. Only by killing her on that plane will they put a permanent stop to her. </div><div><br/></div><div>If the party somehow decides to release the djinn in the jewels (does not require breaking them), the crown can be used to control them. </div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="color:rgb(13, 58, 153);--inversion-type-color:simple;">The Shadowfell</span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>In the shadow realm, the following rules apply: </div><ul><li><div>healing is only half as effective</div></li><li><div>all negative energy attacks are doubled</div></li><li><div>all undead have regeneration 5</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Encounters while the party is searching for the Raven Queen: </div><ul><li><div>A Great Wyrm Red Shadow Dragon (see MM pp 85) + 3 - 5 Shadow Fire Efreet</div></li><li><div>Nightwalker w/ 10+ Shadar Kai</div></li><li><div><a href="https://jsigvard.com/dnd/monster.php?m=Banderhobb" rev="en_rl_none">Banderhobbs</a> sent to assassinate the party as they grew close </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><ul><li><div>5 members of the Atanian nobility are using the gems to manufacture weapons</div></li><li><div>The King publicly orders everyone bring the gems to the Engineering school. </div></li><ul><li><div>The spymaster secretly relays additional orders: bring decoys to the school, bring the real gems to the King’s palace</div></li></ul><li><div>6 gems, each has a Djinn trapped inside of it. The Raven Queen was released from it? </div></li><li><div>The party needs to destroy the Djinn on their native planes (the Elemental Djinn)</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 34</title>
    <created>20201222T064037Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212206Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
