  <note>
    <title>Session 35</title>
    <created>20201222T064037Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212200Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div>The Arch-Dao took the gem that was embedded in the Staff of the Djinn. </div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen teleported to another plane to recover after the staff's retributive strike. </div><div><br/></div><div>Barachiel: release the djinn in their native elemental planes, and by the time you're done, they'll locate the Raven Queen. </div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div>The party faces off with <b>Banrion Fitheach,</b> the Raven Queen. She is in possession of the Staff of the Djinn, which the party has not seen yet. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="color:rgb(4, 51, 255);">The Staff of the Djinn</span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>The Raven Queen will use the staff to summon forth the djinn from the crown, shattering the gems, once per round. Also, in the next round after she starts, a Nightwalker will enter the cave by breaking through the stone. </div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="color:rgb(13, 58, 153);--inversion-type-color:simple;">The Shadowfell</span></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div>In the shadow realm, the following rules apply: </div><ul><li><div>healing is only half as effective</div></li><li><div>all negative energy attacks are doubled</div></li><li><div>all undead have regeneration 5</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Encounters while the party is searching for the Raven Queen: </div><ul><li><div>A Great Wyrm Red Shadow Dragon (see MM pp 85) + 3 - 5 Shadow Fire Efreet</div></li><li><div>Nightwalker w/ 10+ Shadar Kai</div></li><li><div><a href="https://jsigvard.com/dnd/monster.php?m=Banderhobb" rev="en_rl_none">Banderhobbs</a> sent to assassinate the party as they grew close </div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div>####</div><div><br/></div><div><b><span style="font-size: 20px;"><u>Artifacts</u></span></b></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Crown of Darian</b> - Six peaks on the crown hold a jewel each. Each jewel holds a djinn of great power. Each djinn has X abilities and can be invoked as a single action. Legendary actions can be taken between turns to activate the djinn. </div><ul><li><div>5 members of the Atanian nobility are using the gems to manufacture weapons</div></li><li><div>The King publicly orders everyone bring the gems to the Engineering school. </div></li><ul><li><div>The spymaster secretly relays additional orders: bring decoys to the school, bring the real gems to the King’s palace</div></li></ul><li><div>6 gems, each has a Djinn trapped inside of it. The Raven Queen was released from it? </div></li><li><div>The party needs to destroy the Djinn on their native planes (the Elemental Djinn)</div></li></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>The Gem of Djinn Control</b>, originally set in the pommel of the sword, is at the bottom of the ocean, below a 900 foot high cliff. Darian threw the gem into the ocean so that no one would ever use it again, but he now sees that it needs to be retrieved. He made the party promise to destroy the gem after destroying Banrion. </div><div><br/></div><ul><li><div>Gem stats</div></li><ul><li><div>Int 16, Wis 10, Cha 24</div></li><li><div>Communicates via emotion, mostly anger and desire</div></li><li><div>Hearing and dark vision out to 120 feet</div></li><li><div>CN alignment</div></li><li><div>Purpose: to bring the Djinn back under control of the Creator. The gem is an agent of chaos, and even though its purpose is to control the djinn, it might just as easily refuse to cooperate. </div></li><li><div>If a sentient item attempts to take control of its wielder, the wielder must make a Charisma Saving Throw, with a DC equal to 12 + the item’s Charisma modifier. On a failed save, the wielder is Charmed by the item for 1d12 hours. While Charmed, the wielder must try to follow the item’s commands. If the wielder takes damage, it can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the Effect on a success. Whether the attempt to control its user succeeds or fails, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn.</div></li></ul></ul><div><br/></div><div><br/></div><div><b>Staff of the Djinn</b> - As Staff of the Magi + Dominate Monster (Djinn only) 5 charges. </div><div><br/></div><h1 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">Staff of the Magi</span></h1><div style="text-align:start;"><br/></div><div><br/></div><div style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:rgb(68, 68, 68);">Requires </span><a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Attunement" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Attunement</span></a> by a <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Sorcerer#h-Sorcerer" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Sorcerer</span></a>, <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Warlock#h-Warlock" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Warlock</span></a>, or <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Wizard#h-Wizard" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Wizard</span></a>This staff can be wielded as a magic <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Quarterstaff#h-Quarterstaff" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Quarterstaff</span></a> that grants a +2 bonus to <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Combat#h-Attack" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Attack</span></a> and <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Appendix%20B%20-%20Combat#h-Damage%20Rolls" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Damage Rolls</span></a> made with it. While you hold it, you gain a +2 bonus to spell <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Appendix%20B%20-%20Combat#h-Attack%20Rolls" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Attack Rolls</span></a>.The staff has 50 <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> for the following <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Adventuring%20Options#h-Properties" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Properties</span></a>. It regains 4d6 + 2 expended <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20. On a 20, the staff regains 1d12 + 1 <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a>.Spell Absorption: While holding the staff, you have advantage on <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Chapter%202%20-%20Character%20Creation#h-Saving%20Throws" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Saving Throws</span></a> against <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Spells#h-Spells" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Spells</span></a>. In addition, you can use your <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Sorcerer#h-Reaction" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Reaction</span></a> when another creature casts a spell that <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Spells#h-Targets" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Targets</span></a> only you. If you do, the staff absorbs the magic of the spell, canceling its <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Wheel%20of%20Fortune#h-Effect" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Effect</span></a> and gaining a number of <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> equal to the absorbed spell's level. However, if doing so brings the staff's total number of <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> above 50, the staff explodes as if you activated its retributive strike (see below).Spells: While holding the staff, you can use an action to expend some of its <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> to cast one of the following <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Spells#h-Spells" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Spells</span></a> from it, using your spell save DC and <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Spellcasting#h-Spellcasting" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Spellcasting</span></a> ability: <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Conjure%20Elemental#h-Conjure%20Elemental" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Conjure Elemental</span></a> (7 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Dispel%20Magic#h-Dispel%20Magic" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Dispel Magic</span></a> (3 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Fireball#h-Fireball" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Fireball</span></a> (7th-level version, 7 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Flaming%20Sphere#h-Flaming%20Sphere" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Flaming Sphere</span></a> (2 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Ice%20Storm#h-Ice%20Storm" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Ice Storm</span></a> (4 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Invisibility#h-Invisibility" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Invisibility</span></a> (2 charges), knock (2 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Lightning%20Bolt#h-Lightning%20Bolt" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Lightning Bolt</span></a> (7th-level version, 7 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Passwall#h-Passwall" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Passwall</span></a> (5 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Plane%20Shift#h-Plane%20Shift" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Plane Shift</span></a> (7 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Telekinesis#h-Telekinesis" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Telekinesis</span></a> (5 charges), <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Wall%20of%20Fire#h-Wall%20of%20Fire" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Wall of Fire</span></a> (4 charges), or web (2 charges).You can also use an action to cast one of the following <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Spells#h-Spells" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Spells</span></a> from the staff without using any charges: <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Arcane%20Lock#h-Arcane%20Lock" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Arcane Lock</span></a>, <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Detect%20Magic#h-Detect%20Magic" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Detect Magic</span></a>, enlarge/reduce, light, <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Mage%20Hand#h-Mage%20Hand" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Mage Hand</span></a>, or <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Protection%20from%20Evil%20and%20Good#h-Protection%20from%20Evil%20and%20Good" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Protection from Evil and Good</span></a>.Retributive Strike: You can use an action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface, performing a retributive strike. The staff is destroyed and releases its remaining magic in an explosion that expands to fill a 30-foot-radius <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Spells#h-Sphere" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Sphere</span></a> centered on it.You have a 50 percent chance to instantly <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Travel#h-Travel" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Travel</span></a> to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion. If you fail to avoid the <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Wheel%20of%20Fortune#h-Effect" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Effect</span></a>, you take force damage equal to 16 x the number of <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> in the staff. Every other creature in the area must make a DC 17 <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Ability%20Scores#h-Dexterity" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Dexterity</span></a> saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes an amount of damage based on how far away it is from the point of <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Outlander#h-Origin" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Origin</span></a>, as shown in the following table. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage.Distance from <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Outlander#h-Origin" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Origin</span></a> — Damage:10 ft. away or closer — 8 x the number of <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> in the staff11 to 20 ft. away — 6 x the number of <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> in the staff21 to 30 ft. away — 4 x the number of <a href="https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Magic%20Items#h-Charges" rev="en_rl_none"><span style="color:rgb(65, 143, 222);">Charges</span></a> in the staff</div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
  <note>
    <title>Session 15</title>
    <created>20200211T232044Z</created>
    <updated>20210306T212138Z</updated>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>Cory Huff</author>
      <source>desktop.mac</source>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd"><en-note><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">Brain raped by a fairy dragon. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">Very angry wet cat. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">“I fart out my nose.” </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">####</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></div><div>
<span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">A powerful fey conjurer, Cruthaigh, will reach through where the portal was created, angry at the party for stealing his mastodon. That portal will be how the party gets out of the dragon cave. If they take the portal, Finnleik will sprint for the portal, trying to escape with them. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span></div><div><font face="Helvetica Neue" style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">The mastodon begins opening portals home, but accidentally opens portals to multiple locations, allowing a variety of constructs to enter the lair, and for the party to exit via the same portals, leading to a variety of locations.  </span></font></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span></div><div><br/></div><div><font face="Helvetica Neue" style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="white-space: pre; font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">	</span><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">Rutherford’s Mansion > trigger Zel’s return &amp; a hunt for Silvermane </span></font></div><ul><ul><li><div>Tur’og, the orcish commander, has imposed martial law and begun rebuilding the city after Zel destroyed a huge swatch with his acid breath. </div></li><li><div>The Runegate has a crack in it from the explosion. Unknown to the orcs, demonic elements and Unseelie Fey have crept into Ghealdar through the gate. </div></li><li><div>Zel is definitely dead, according to everyone. They just finished cleaning up the vestiges of his carcass. </div></li><ul><li><div>Zel is not dead. He has risen as a shadow dragon in the swamps outside Ghealdar. Many goblins have converted to worshipping the Raven Queen, or have been killed by the dragon’s breath and live as shadows in the swamp. </div></li></ul></ul></ul><div><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span></div><div><br/></div><div><font face="Helvetica Neue" style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="white-space: pre; font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">	</span><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">Cruthaigh’s home in the Feywild > trigger golem battles and escape into the Feywild </span></font></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
Upon realizing who Cro is, Cruthaigh, Cog’s creator, shows up to reclaim ownership of Cog, and the party might need to protect him. The wizard’s minions attack the party but gets attacked by the Raven Queen. When Cruthaigh begins taking control of Cro’s will, Cro will need to decide which master he will serve. </span></div><div><font face="Helvetica Neue" style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="white-space: pre; font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">	</span><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">Flesh Golem (MM 170), 1800 xp </span></font></div><div><font face="Helvetica Neue" style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></font></div><div><font face="Helvetica Neue" style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;"><br/></span></font></div><div><span style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times; -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times; -webkit-font-kerning: none; font-stretch: normal; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; line-height: normal;">
</span></div></en-note>      ]]>
    </content>
  </note>
</en-export>
